{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BmDYYu49KzhxTXnPwKpiRH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-2035-gkr-input-round-robin\n2\t\n3\tReplace contiguous work chunking in GKR input evaluation with interleaved (round-robin) assignment across multi-stream threads. Currently, work items are sorted by descending trace height and split into contiguous chunks via `work_items.chunks(chunk_size)`, causing thread 0 to receive all large AIRs and thread 7 to receive only tiny AIRs. This is the same load imbalance pattern that the Round 0 round-robin optimization fixed (saving 36ms / 1.13x at APC 300). With round-robin assignment, each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs, reducing the critical thread's wall time and enabling better GPU-stream overlap. At APC 300, GKR input eval is 318ms total (seg0=256ms, seg1=62ms); improved load balance should save 10-25ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"e7440c48-5436-4d7d-8c3f-5d826008f276","timestamp":"2026-04-13T19:44:32.917Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2035-gkr-input-round-robin\n\nReplace contiguous work chunking in GKR input evaluation with interleaved (round-robin) assignment across multi-stream threads. Currently, work items are sorted by descending trace height and split into contiguous chunks via `work_items.chunks(chunk_size)`, causing thread 0 to receive all large AIRs and thread 7 to receive only tiny AIRs. This is the same load imbalance pattern that the Round 0 round-robin optimization fixed (saving 36ms / 1.13x at APC 300). With round-robin assignment, each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs, reducing the critical thread's wall time and enabling better GPU-stream overlap. At APC 300, GKR input eval is 318ms total (seg0=256ms, seg1=62ms); improved load balance should save 10-25ms.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
