fer with zeros before scattering traces\n   - This happens ONLY if caching stacked matrix OR during rs_code_matrix\n\n2. Memory allocations in rs_code_matrix()\n   - DeviceBuffer allocation at line 194 (codewords buffer)\n   \n3. Memory allocations in merkle tree\n   - query_digest_layer allocation at line 127\n   - layer allocations in loop at line 145\n\n## Synchronization Points\n\n1. After stack_columns() kernel (line 170)\n2. After each compress_rows() kernel (line 130-137)\n3. After each compress_layer() kernel (line 152)\n4. D2H transfer of root (line 163)\n\n## Per-AIR vs Per-Segment Breakdown\n\nFrom the code analysis:\n- rs_code_matrix() is called ONCE per commit (line 70)\n- stacked_commit() is called by TraceCommitter::commit() (gpu_backend.rs:65)\n- This is called by the Coordinator for each trace commitment phase\n- Multiple AIRs may be committed in sequence or batched\n\nThe stacked matrix contains ALL traces (line 53: traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>])\nSo the poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel operates on:\n- width = total width of stacked matrix\n- height = stacked height (2^(l_skip + n_stack))\n- query_stride = height / rows_per_query\n\nThe Nsight observation of \"25 instances\" suggests:\n- Multiple kernel launches for different commits/AIRs\n- Or internal kernel launch batches by the CUDA driver","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017xfWakUxcTtEsGZ6gBJyh2","session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"7e853eaa-2061-4d30-801c-746888be8336","timestamp":"2026-04-13T19:58:06.933Z"}
