{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F6BHXgyRZqHEtXgykifv6U","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summary: Round 0 and LogUp GKR Code Paths in CUDA Backend\n\nBased on my thorough analysis of the codebase, here's the complete architectural breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## ROUND 0 ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Main Entry Point: `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n\nThis function orchestrates Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation across all AIRs using **multi-threaded GPU streams**. The architecture consists of 3 main phases:\n\n#### **Phase 1: Build Work Items (lines 899-926)**\n- Creates `Round0AirWorkItem` structs for each present AIR (trace_idx, pk data, selectors, public values, eq evaluations, etc.)\n- Each work item captures all read-only references needed for one AIR's processing\n- Work items are **sorted by descending height** for load balancing\n\n#### **Phase 2: Multi-Threaded AIR Processing (lines 928-986)**\n\n**Thread Pool Configuration:**\n- Uses up to `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS = 8` OS threads (defined at line 95)\n- Thread allocation logic at lines 939-943:\n  - Uses multiple threads only when `work_items.len() >= 100` (heuristic to avoid overhead)\n  - Maximum threads = `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())`\n  - Falls back to single-threaded for small AIR counts\n\n**Distribution Strategy (lines 950-961):**\n- **Interleaved (round-robin)** assignment: Thread i gets items at indices `[i, i+N, i+2N, ...]`\n- This balances large and small AIRs across threads despite height-sorted order\n- Each thread operates on its own CUDA stream (implicit via OS thread affinity)\n\n**Per-AIR Work (`process_air_round0`, lines 140-272):**\n\nThe worker thread processes each AIR in sequence:\n\n1. **Plain Constraints Evaluation** (lines 168-181):\n   - Calls `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` which:\n     - Kernel: `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` (CUDA kernel in `logup_zerocheck.rs:351`)\n     - Evaluates symbolic constraint DAG at coset domain points\n     - Returns `sum_buffer` with EF values (sumcheck polynomial evals)\n\n2. **Interaction Constraints Evaluation** (lines 213-229):\n   - Calls `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` which:\n     - Kernel: `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` (CUDA kernel in `logup_zerocheck.rs:311`)\n     - Evaluates interaction count + message expressions using barycentric interpolation\n     - Returns `sum` buffer with `Frac<EF>` values (fractional sumcheck input)\n\n3. **D2H Copy + Post-processing** (lines 183-271):\n   - Copies results to host on current stream (synchronous)\n   - IDFT to convert coset evals to coefficients\n   - Constructs univariate polynomials for logup numerator/denominator\n   - Returns `Round0AirResult` with up to 3 polynomials\n\n#### **Phase 3: Scatter Results (lines 988-1003)**\n- Collects results from all threads\n- Scatters polynomials into `batch_sp_poly` vector for downstream sumcheck rounds\n- Layout: `[logup_numer_0, logup_denom_0, logup_numer_1, logup_denom_1, ..., zc_0, zc_1, ...]`\n\n### Batched Round 0 Kernels\n\nThere are **NO batched Round 0 descriptor array kernels** (no `batched_zerocheck_r0`, `Round0ZcCtx`, `round0_batched`). Instead:\n\n- **Per-AIR kernels** (`zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`, `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`)\n- Each thread dispatches one kernel per AIR sequentially\n- Kernels run on **separate CUDA streams** (one per thread) for parallelism\n- Memory allocation: Per-thread `max_temp_bytes` budget (lines 900, 924)\n\n### Key Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Location | Purpose |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `skip_domain` | line 175 | `1 << l_skip` - interpolation skip domain size |\n| `num_x` | line 176 | `1 << n_lift` - number of constraint evaluation points |\n| `num_cosets` | line 178 | `local_constraint_deg - 1` for zerocheck, `constraint_degree` for logup |\n| `g_shift` | line 179 | `omega_root` - generator shift for coset evaluation |\n| `max_temp_bytes` | line 924 | Per-thread memory budget (subset of `memory_limit_bytes`) |\n\n---\n\n## LOGUP GKR ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Main Entry Point: `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:276-574`\n\nThe GKR code path consists of two logical stages:\n\n#### **Stage 1: GKR Input Evaluation** (lines 345-371)\n\n**Function:** `log_gkr_input_evals`\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs:215-354`\n\nEvaluates interaction expressions from traces to produce (p, q) fractional polynomial leaves.\n\n**Sub-Stage 1a: Build Work Items (lines 231-250)**\n- Creates `GkrInputWorkItem` for each trace with interactions\n- Extracts stacked layout info, destination pointers in leaves buffer\n- Sorts by descending height for load balance\n\n**Sub-Stage 1b: Pre-compute Buffer Sizes (lines 254-279)**\n- Computes max intermediates, public_values, partition_ptrs, and tmp buffers across all AIRs\n- Used to pre-allocate per-thread buffer pools\n\n**Sub-Stage 1c: Memory Budget Check (lines 285-303)**\n- Dynamically reduces thread count if per-thread allocation exceeds 2 GB\n- Prevents excessive GPU memory usage\n\n**Sub-Stage 1d: Multi-Threaded GKR Input Processing (lines 306-349)**\n\n**Thread Configuration:**\n- Up to `NUM_GKR_INPUT_STREAMS = 8` threads (defined at line 30)\n- Multi-threading only if `work_items.len() >= 100` (line 286)\n- Thread count can be further reduced for large AIRs\n\n**Per-AIR Work (`process_gkr_input_air`, lines 112-210):**\n\n1. **Kernel Launch** (line 174):\n   - Calls `logup_gkr_input_eval` CUDA kernel\n   - Kernel: `_logup_gkr_input_eval` (declared at `logup_zerocheck.rs:278`)\n   - Parameters:\n     - `is_global`: bool flag based on `buffer_size > 10`\n     - `trace_output`: destination buffer (leaves_ptr or tmp buffer)\n     - `d_preprocessed`, `d_public_values`, `challenges`: trace inputs\n     - `intermediates`, `d_rules`, `d_used_nodes`, `pair_idxs`: DAG evaluation context\n     - `height`, `num_rows_per_tile`: tiling parameters (TASK_SIZE = 65536)\n\n2. **Post-processing for Height Lift** (lines 189-207):\n   - If trace height < lifted_height: normalize and vertically repeat\n   - Ensures all traces align to lifted domain size\n\n**Output:** `(leaves, alpha_logup)` - fractional polynomial leaf buffer\n\n#### **Stage 2: GKR Body (Fractional Sumcheck)** (lines 373-381)\n\n**Function:** `fractional_sumcheck_gpu`\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs:491-1020`\n\nExecutes GKR fractional sumcheck rounds on the leaves buffer.\n\n**Per-AIR Scope:** \n- **NOT per-AIR** - runs on **unified leaves buffer** from all traces\n- **Single stream** operation (all kernels on default CUDA stream)\n\n**Architecture:**\n\n1. **Segment Tree Construction** (lines 517-576):\n   - Builds binary tree via repeated \"layer\" computations\n   - Fuses bitrev + layers 0+1 for large inputs (> 1024 leaves)\n   - Two-layer kernels for efficiency (lines 561-568)\n   - Output: segment tree rooted at single value\n\n2. **GKR Round Loop** (lines 655-1010):\n   - **Outer rounds:** One per GKR variable (1..total_rounds = l_skip + n_logup)\n   - **For each outer round:**\n     - Samples lambda challenge\n     - Calls either:\n       - **FoldEval Strategy** (lines 718-819): Fused compute + fold in 1+ inner rounds\n       - **PrecomputeM Strategy** (lines 821-1010): Window-based precomputation for large rounds\n\n**Key Kernel Variants:**\n\n| Operation | Kernel | Location |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| Round 0 (revert) | `frac_compute_round_and_revert` | line 698, cuda 144 |\n| Compute + fold (oop) | `frac_compute_round_and_fold` | line 726, cuda 165 |\n| Compute + fold (ip) | `frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace` | line 758, cuda 181 |\n| Precompute-M build | `frac_precompute_m_build` | line ~900, cuda 193 |\n| Precompute-M eval | `frac_precompute_m_eval_round` | line ~920, cuda 209 |\n| Multifold | `frac_multifold` | line ~950, cuda 218 |\n| Final fold | `fold_ef_frac_columns_inplace` | line 798, cuda 155 |\n\n**Buffer Strategy:**\n- Two buffers: `layer` (input/output) and `work_buffer` (intermediate)\n- Ping-pong for memory efficiency, in-place when possible\n\n**Output:** `(FracSumcheckProof, Vec<EF>)` - GKR proof and sampled challenges (xi)\n\n---\n\n## COMPARISON: Round 0 vs GKR\n\n| Aspect | Round 0 | GKR Body |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| **Scope** | Per-AIR | All AIRs (unified buffer) |\n| **Threading** | Multi-threaded (8 streams) | Single-threaded (1 stream) |\n| **Kernels** | Constraint/interaction evaluation | Segment tree + sumcheck rounds |\n| **Distribution** | Interleaved load balance | N/A (unified data) |\n| **Memory** | Per-thread budgets | Global budget (set after input eval) |\n| **Synchronization** | Thread barriers + D2H syncs | Current stream syncs |\n| **Batched Kernels** | None (per-AIR only) | Fused compute+fold variants |\n\n---\n\n## FILE REFERENCE GUIDE\n\n| Task | File | Lines |\n|------|------|-------|\n| Main orchestration | `mod.rs` | 276-574 |\n| Round 0 implementation | `round0.rs` | 31-275 |\n| Round 0 orchestration | `mod.rs` | 767-1003 |\n| GKR input evals | `gkr_input.rs` | 215-354 |\n| GKR body/sumcheck | `fractional.rs` | 491-1020 |\n| Batch MLE (later rounds) | `batch_mle.rs` | 414-502, 505-600+ |\n| CUDA kernel declarations | `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` | 114-539 |\n| Kernel context types | `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` | 8-111 |\n\n---\n\n## Critical No-Op Infrastructure\n\n**Removed:** No batched Round 0 descriptor array infrastructure (`batched_zerocheck_r0`, `Round0ZcCtx`, `round0_batched`) exists. The design uses:\n- Per-AIR sequential kernels\n- OS-thread-based parallelism (not CUDA thread-block parallelism)\n- This is fundamentally different from the batched monomial/MLE kernels used in later sumcheck rounds"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"474a6a37-af8f-4ddc-9cdd-6d77cfc26724","timestamp":"2026-04-13T19:58:11.053Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the current state of the Round 0 and LogUp GKR code paths in the CUDA backend. Focus on `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/` directory.\n\nFor Round 0:\n1. Find the main function for Round 0 constraint evaluation (likely `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` in `mod.rs`)\n2. How does the multi-stream threading work? How are AIRs distributed across threads?\n3. What does each thread do per-AIR? (kernel launches, D2H copies, post-processing)\n4. Are there any existing batched Round 0 CUDA kernels or descriptor array infrastructure remaining in the code? Check for `batched_zerocheck_r0`, `Round0ZcCtx`, `round0_batched`, etc.\n\nFor LogUp GKR:\n1. Find the main GKR entry point (likely `log_gkr` or similar function)\n2. What's the split between \"GKR input evaluation\" and \"GKR body\" (the sumcheck rounds)?\n3. For the GKR body: is it per-AIR? per-segment? Does it run on a single stream or multiple?\n4. Look for the `fractional_sumcheck_gkr` CUDA kernel calls and find their Rust callers\n\nReport file paths and line numbers for key functions and loops. Be thorough — I need to understand the architecture of both code paths.","agentId":"a13100ed9f286fd83","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summary: Round 0 and LogUp GKR Code Paths in CUDA Backend\n\nBased on my thorough analysis of the codebase, here's the complete architectural breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## ROUND 0 ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Main Entry Point: `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n\nThis function orchestrates Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation across all AIRs using **multi-threaded GPU streams**. The architecture consists of 3 main phases:\n\n#### **Phase 1: Build Work Items (lines 899-926)**\n- Creates `Round0AirWorkItem` structs for each present AIR (trace_idx, pk data, selectors, public values, eq evaluations, etc.)\n- Each work item captures all read-only references needed for one AIR's processing\n- Work items are **sorted by descending height** for load balancing\n\n#### **Phase 2: Multi-Threaded AIR Processing (lines 928-986)**\n\n**Thread Pool Configuration:**\n- Uses up to `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS = 8` OS threads (defined at line 95)\n- Thread allocation logic at lines 939-943:\n  - Uses multiple threads only when `work_items.len() >= 100` (heuristic to avoid overhead)\n  - Maximum threads = `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())`\n  - Falls back to single-threaded for small AIR counts\n\n**Distribution Strategy (lines 950-961):**\n- **Interleaved (round-robin)** assignment: Thread i gets items at indices `[i, i+N, i+2N, ...]`\n- This balances large and small AIRs across threads despite height-sorted order\n- Each thread operates on its own CUDA stream (implicit via OS thread affinity)\n\n**Per-AIR Work (`process_air_round0`, lines 140-272):**\n\nThe worker thread processes each AIR in sequence:\n\n1. **Plain Constraints Evaluation** (lines 168-181):\n   - Calls `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` which:\n     - Kernel: `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` (CUDA kernel in `logup_zerocheck.rs:351`)\n     - Evaluates symbolic constraint DAG at coset domain points\n     - Returns `sum_buffer` with EF values (sumcheck polynomial evals)\n\n2. **Interaction Constraints Evaluation** (lines 213-229):\n   - Calls `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` which:\n     - Kernel: `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` (CUDA kernel in `logup_zerocheck.rs:311`)\n     - Evaluates interaction count + message expressions using barycentric interpolation\n     - Returns `sum` buffer with `Frac<EF>` values (fractional sumcheck input)\n\n3. **D2H Copy + Post-processing** (lines 183-271):\n   - Copies results to host on current stream (synchronous)\n   - IDFT to convert coset evals to coefficients\n   - Constructs univariate polynomials for logup numerator/denominator\n   - Returns `Round0AirResult` with up to 3 polynomials\n\n#### **Phase 3: Scatter Results (lines 988-1003)**\n- Collects results from all threads\n- Scatters polynomials into `batch_sp_poly` vector for downstream sumcheck rounds\n- Layout: `[logup_numer_0, logup_denom_0, logup_numer_1, logup_denom_1, ..., zc_0, zc_1, ...]`\n\n### Batched Round 0 Kernels\n\nThere are **NO batched Round 0 descriptor array kernels** (no `batched_zerocheck_r0`, `Round0ZcCtx`, `round0_batched`). Instead:\n\n- **Per-AIR kernels** (`zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`, `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`)\n- Each thread dispatches one kernel per AIR sequentially\n- Kernels run on **separate CUDA streams** (one per thread) for parallelism\n- Memory allocation: Per-thread `max_temp_bytes` budget (lines 900, 924)\n\n### Key Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Location | Purpose |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `skip_domain` | line 175 | `1 << l_skip` - interpolation skip domain size |\n| `num_x` | line 176 | `1 << n_lift` - number of constraint evaluation points |\n| `num_cosets` | line 178 | `local_constraint_deg - 1` for zerocheck, `constraint_degree` for logup |\n| `g_shift` | line 179 | `omega_root` - generator shift for coset evaluation |\n| `max_temp_bytes` | line 924 | Per-thread memory budget (subset of `memory_limit_bytes`) |\n\n---\n\n## LOGUP GKR ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Main Entry Point: `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:276-574`\n\nThe GKR code path consists of two logical stages:\n\n#### **Stage 1: GKR Input Evaluation** (lines 345-371)\n\n**Function:** `log_gkr_input_evals`\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs:215-354`\n\nEvaluates interaction expressions from traces to produce (p, q) fractional polynomial leaves.\n\n**Sub-Stage 1a: Build Work Items (lines 231-250)**\n- Creates `GkrInputWorkItem` for each trace with interactions\n- Extracts stacked layout info, destination pointers in leaves buffer\n- Sorts by descending height for load balance\n\n**Sub-Stage 1b: Pre-compute Buffer Sizes (lines 254-279)**\n- Computes max intermediates, public_values, partition_ptrs, and tmp buffers across all AIRs\n- Used to pre-allocate per-thread buffer pools\n\n**Sub-Stage 1c: Memory Budget Check (lines 285-303)**\n- Dynamically reduces thread count if per-thread allocation exceeds 2 GB\n- Prevents excessive GPU memory usage\n\n**Sub-Stage 1d: Multi-Threaded GKR Input Processing (lines 306-349)**\n\n**Thread Configuration:**\n- Up to `NUM_GKR_INPUT_STREAMS = 8` threads (defined at line 30)\n- Multi-threading only if `work_items.len() >= 100` (line 286)\n- Thread count can be further reduced for large AIRs\n\n**Per-AIR Work (`process_gkr_input_air`, lines 112-210):**\n\n1. **Kernel Launch** (line 174):\n   - Calls `logup_gkr_input_eval` CUDA kernel\n   - Kernel: `_logup_gkr_input_eval` (declared at `logup_zerocheck.rs:278`)\n   - Parameters:\n     - `is_global`: bool flag based on `buffer_size > 10`\n     - `trace_output`: destination buffer (leaves_ptr or tmp buffer)\n     - `d_preprocessed`, `d_public_values`, `challenges`: trace inputs\n     - `intermediates`, `d_rules`, `d_used_nodes`, `pair_idxs`: DAG evaluation context\n     - `height`, `num_rows_per_tile`: tiling parameters (TASK_SIZE = 65536)\n\n2. **Post-processing for Height Lift** (lines 189-207):\n   - If trace height < lifted_height: normalize and vertically repeat\n   - Ensures all traces align to lifted domain size\n\n**Output:** `(leaves, alpha_logup)` - fractional polynomial leaf buffer\n\n#### **Stage 2: GKR Body (Fractional Sumcheck)** (lines 373-381)\n\n**Function:** `fractional_sumcheck_gpu`\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs:491-1020`\n\nExecutes GKR fractional sumcheck rounds on the leaves buffer.\n\n**Per-AIR Scope:** \n- **NOT per-AIR** - runs on **unified leaves buffer** from all traces\n- **Single stream** operation (all kernels on default CUDA stream)\n\n**Architecture:**\n\n1. **Segment Tree Construction** (lines 517-576):\n   - Builds binary tree via repeated \"layer\" computations\n   - Fuses bitrev + layers 0+1 for large inputs (> 1024 leaves)\n   - Two-layer kernels for efficiency (lines 561-568)\n   - Output: segment tree rooted at single value\n\n2. **GKR Round Loop** (lines 655-1010):\n   - **Outer rounds:** One per GKR variable (1..total_rounds = l_skip + n_logup)\n   - **For each outer round:**\n     - Samples lambda challenge\n     - Calls either:\n       - **FoldEval Strategy** (lines 718-819): Fused compute + fold in 1+ inner rounds\n       - **PrecomputeM Strategy** (lines 821-1010): Window-based precomputation for large rounds\n\n**Key Kernel Variants:**\n\n| Operation | Kernel | Location |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| Round 0 (revert) | `frac_compute_round_and_revert` | line 698, cuda 144 |\n| Compute + fold (oop) | `frac_compute_round_and_fold` | line 726, cuda 165 |\n| Compute + fold (ip) | `frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace` | line 758, cuda 181 |\n| Precompute-M build | `frac_precompute_m_build` | line ~900, cuda 193 |\n| Precompute-M eval | `frac_precompute_m_eval_round` | line ~920, cuda 209 |\n| Multifold | `frac_multifold` | line ~950, cuda 218 |\n| Final fold | `fold_ef_frac_columns_inplace` | line 798, cuda 155 |\n\n**Buffer Strategy:**\n- Two buffers: `layer` (input/output) and `work_buffer` (intermediate)\n- Ping-pong for memory efficiency, in-place when possible\n\n**Output:** `(FracSumcheckProof, Vec<EF>)` - GKR proof and sampled challenges (xi)\n\n---\n\n## COMPARISON: Round 0 vs GKR\n\n| Aspect | Round 0 | GKR Body |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| **Scope** | Per-AIR | All AIRs (unified buffer) |\n| **Threading** | Multi-threaded (8 streams) | Single-threaded (1 stream) |\n| **Kernels** | Constraint/interaction evaluation | Segment tree + sumcheck rounds |\n| **Distribution** | Interleaved load balance | N/A (unified data) |\n| **Memory** | Per-thread budgets | Global budget (set after input eval) |\n| **Synchronization** | Thread barriers + D2H syncs | Current stream syncs |\n| **Batched Kernels** | None (per-AIR only) | Fused compute+fold variants |\n\n---\n\n## FILE REFERENCE GUIDE\n\n| Task | File | Lines |\n|------|------|-------|\n| Main orchestration | `mod.rs` | 276-574 |\n| Round 0 implementation | `round0.rs` | 31-275 |\n| Round 0 orchestration | `mod.rs` | 767-1003 |\n| GKR input evals | `gkr_input.rs` | 215-354 |\n| GKR body/sumcheck | `fractional.rs` | 491-1020 |\n| Batch MLE (later rounds) | `batch_mle.rs` | 414-502, 505-600+ |\n| CUDA kernel declarations | `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` | 114-539 |\n| Kernel context types | `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` | 8-111 |\n\n---\n\n## Critical No-Op Infrastructure\n\n**Removed:** No batched Round 0 descriptor array infrastructure (`batched_zerocheck_r0`, `Round0ZcCtx`, `round0_batched`) exists. The design uses:\n- Per-AIR sequential kernels\n- OS-thread-based parallelism (not CUDA thread-block parallelism)\n- This is fundamentally different from the batched monomial/MLE kernels used in later sumcheck rounds"}],"totalDurationMs":73307,"totalTokens":78449,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_read_input_tokens":73706,"output_tokens":3184,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1555},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3184,"cache_read_input_tokens":73706,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cac