{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MgQca5zp61RMg4N9GLzjwu","type":"tool_result","content":"215\tpub fn log_gkr_input_evals<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n216\t    trace_interactions: &[Option<TraceInteractionMeta>],\n217\t    pk: &DeviceMultiStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n218\t    ctx: &ProvingContext<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n219\t    l_skip: usize,\n220\t    alpha_logup: EF,\n221\t    d_challenges: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n222\t    total_leaves: usize,\n223\t) -> Result<(DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, EF), InteractionGpuError> {\n224\t    if trace_interactions.iter().all(|meta| meta.is_none()) {\n225\t        return Ok((DeviceBuffer::new(), alpha_logup));\n226\t    }\n227\t\n228\t    let leaves = DeviceBuffer::<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(total_leaves);\n229\t    leaves.fill_zero()?;\n230\t\n231\t    // Phase 1: Build work items and sort by descending height for load balance.\n232\t    let mut work_items: Vec<GkrInputWorkItem<HS>> = trace_interactions\n233\t        .iter()\n234\t        .flatten()\n235\t        .map(|meta| {\n236\t            let air_ctx = &ctx.per_trace[meta.trace_idx].1;\n237\t            let pk_air = &pk.per_air[meta.air_idx];\n238\t            let slice = meta.layout_slices.first().unwrap();\n239\t            assert_eq!(slice.col_idx, 0);\n240\t            let dst_offset = slice.row_idx;\n241\t            let leaves_ptr = unsafe { leaves.as_mut_ptr().add(dst_offset) };\n242\t            GkrInputWorkItem {\n243\t                air_ctx,\n244\t                pk_air,\n245\t                l_skip,\n246\t                d_challenges,\n247\t                leaves_ptr: SendPtr(leaves_ptr),\n248\t            }\n249\t        })\n250\t        .collect();\n251\t\n252\t    work_items.sort_by(|a, b| b.air_ctx.height().cmp(&a.air_ctx.height()));\n253\t\n254\t    // Pre-compute max buffer sizes across all work items.\n255\t    let mut max_intermediates_len: usize = 1;\n256\t    let mut max_public_values_len: usize = 0;\n257\t    let mut max_partition_ptrs_len: usize = 0;\n258\t    let mut max_tmp_len: usize = 0;\n259\t\n260\t    for w in &work_items {\n261\t        let rules = &w.pk_air.other_data.interaction_rules;\n262\t        let buffer_size = rules.inner.buffer_size as usize;\n263\t        let is_global = buffer_size > 10;\n264\t        if is_global {\n265\t            max_intermediates_len = max_intermediates_len.max(TASK_SIZE as usize * buffer_size);\n266\t        }\n267\t\n268\t        max_public_values_len = max_public_values_len.max(w.air_ctx.public_values.len());\n269\t\n270\t        let num_partitions = w.air_ctx.cached_mains.len() + 1;\n271\t        max_partition_ptrs_len = max_partition_ptrs_len.max(num_partitions);\n272\t\n273\t        let height = w.air_ctx.height();\n274\t        let lifted_height = height.max(1 << w.l_skip);\n275\t        if height != lifted_height {\n276\t            let num_interactions = w.pk_air.vk.symbolic_constraints.interactions.len();\n277\t            max_tmp_len = max_tmp_len.max(height * num_interactions);\n278\t        }\n279\t    }\n280\t\n281\t    // Barrier: ensure fill_zero() and all prior GPU work is visible to worker thread streams.\n282\t    current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n283\t\n284\t    // Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel across N OS threads.\n285\t    let mut num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n286\t        NUM_GKR_INPUT_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n287\t    } else {\n288\t        1\n289\t    };\n290\t\n291\t    // Memory budget check: reduce num_threads if pre-allocation would exceed 2 GB.\n292\t    let per_thread_bytes = max_intermediates_len * std::mem::size_of::<EF>()\n293\t        + max_public_values_len * std::mem::size_of::<F>()\n294\t        + max_partition_ptrs_len * std::mem::size_of::<u64>()\n295\t        + max_tmp_len * std::mem::size_of::<Frac<EF>>();\n296\t    while num_threads > 1 && num_threads * per_thread_bytes > 2_000_000_000 {\n297\t        num_threads /= 2;\n298\t        tracing::warn!(\n299\t            \"Reducing GKR input eval thread count to {} due to memory budget ({}MB per thread)\",\n300\t            num_threads,\n301\t            per_thread_bytes / (1024 * 1024)\n302\t        );\n303\t    }\n304\t\n305\t    // Pre-allocate per-thread buffer pools to avoid per-AIR mutex contention.\n306\t    let thread_buffers: Vec<GkrThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n307\t        .map(|_| GkrThreadBuffers {\n308\t            intermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_intermediates_len),\n309\t            public_values: if max_public_values_len > 0 {\n310\t                DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_public_values_len)\n311\t            } else {\n312\t                DeviceBuffer::new()\n313\t            },\n314\t            partition_ptrs: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_partition_ptrs_len),\n315\t            tmp: if max_tmp_len > 0 {\n316\t                DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_tmp_len)\n317\t            } else {\n318\t                DeviceBuffer::new()\n319\t            },\n320\t        })\n321\t        .collect();\n322\t\n323\t    if num_threads <= 1 {\n324\t        let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n325\t        for w in &work_items {\n326\t            process_gkr_input_air(w, &mut bufs)?;\n327\t        }\n328\t    } else {\n329\t        let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n330\t        std::thread::scope(|s| {\n331\t            let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n332\t                .into_iter()\n333\t                .zip(work_items.chunks(chunk_size))\n334\t                .map(|(mut bufs, chunk)| {\n335\t                    s.spawn(move || -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n336\t                        for w in chunk {\n337\t                            process_gkr_input_air(w, &mut bufs)?;\n338\t                        }\n339\t                        current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n340\t                        Ok(())\n341\t                    })\n342\t                })\n343\t                .collect();\n344\t            for handle in handles {\n345\t                handle.join().unwrap()?;\n346\t            }\n347\t            Ok::<_, InteractionGpuError>(())\n348\t        })?;\n349\t    }\n350\t\n351\t    // NOTE: alpha is NO LONGER applied here - it will be fused into the first tree layer\n352\t    // in fractional_sumcheck_gpu for better performance (eliminates one memory pass)\n353\t    Ok((leaves, alpha_logup))\n354\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"482f073f-d2c4-4f7a-93fd-149dea84a835","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:12:17.715Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs","content":"pub fn log_gkr_input_evals<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    trace_interactions: &[Option<TraceInteractionMeta>],\n    pk: &DeviceMultiStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    ctx: &ProvingContext<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    l_skip: usize,\n    alpha_logup: EF,\n    d_challenges: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    total_leaves: usize,\n) -> Result<(DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, EF), InteractionGpuError> {\n    if trace_interactions.iter().all(|meta| meta.is_none()) {\n        return Ok((DeviceBuffer::new(), alpha_logup));\n    }\n\n    let leaves = DeviceBuffer::<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(total_leaves);\n    leaves.fill_zero()?;\n\n    // Phase 1: Build work items and sort by descending height for load balance.\n    let mut work_items: Vec<GkrInputWorkItem<HS>> = trace_interactions\n        .iter()\n        .flatten()\n        .map(|meta| {\n            let air_ctx = &ctx.per_trace[meta.trace_idx].1;\n            let pk_air = &pk.per_air[meta.air_idx];\n            let slice = meta.layout_slices.first().unwrap();\n            assert_eq!(slice.col_idx, 0);\n            let dst_offset = slice.row_idx;\n            let leaves_ptr = unsafe { leaves.as_mut_ptr().add(dst_offset) };\n            GkrInputWorkItem {\n                air_ctx,\n                pk_air,\n                l_skip,\n                d_challenges,\n                leaves_ptr: SendPtr(leaves_ptr),\n            }\n        })\n        .collect();\n\n    work_items.sort_by(|a, b| b.air_ctx.height().cmp(&a.air_ctx.height()));\n\n    // Pre-compute max buffer sizes across all work items.\n    let mut max_intermediates_len: usize = 1;\n    let mut max_public_values_len: usize = 0;\n    let mut max_partition_ptrs_len: usize = 0;\n    let mut max_tmp_len: usize = 0;\n\n    for w in &work_items {\n        let rules = &w.pk_air.other_data.interaction_rules;\n        let buffer_size = rules.inner.buffer_size as usize;\n        let is_global = buffer_size > 10;\n        if is_global {\n            max_intermediates_len = max_intermediates_len.max(TASK_SIZE as usize * buffer_size);\n        }\n\n        max_public_values_len = max_public_values_len.max(w.air_ctx.public_values.len());\n\n        let num_partitions = w.air_ctx.cached_mains.len() + 1;\n        max_partition_ptrs_len = max_partition_ptrs_len.max(num_partitions);\n\n        let height = w.air_ctx.height();\n        let lifted_height = height.max(1 << w.l_skip);\n        if height != lifted_height {\n            let num_interactions = w.pk_air.vk.symbolic_constraints.interactions.len();\n            max_tmp_len = max_tmp_len.max(height * num_interactions);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Barrier: ensure fill_zero() and all prior GPU work is visible to worker thread streams.\n    current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n\n    // Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel across N OS threads.\n    let mut num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n        NUM_GKR_INPUT_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n    } else {\n        1\n    };\n\n    // Memory budget check: reduce num_threads if pre-allocation would exceed 2 GB.\n    let per_thread_bytes = max_intermediates_len * std::mem::size_of::<EF>()\n        + max_public_values_len * std::mem::size_of::<F>()\n        + max_partition_ptrs_len * std::mem::size_of::<u64>()\n        + max_tmp_len * std::mem::size_of::<Frac<EF>>();\n    while num_threads > 1 && num_threads * per_thread_bytes > 2_000_000_000 {\n        num_threads /= 2;\n        tracing::warn!(\n            \"Reducing GKR input eval thread count to {} due to memory budget ({}MB per thread)\",\n            num_threads,\n            per_thread_bytes / (1024 * 1024)\n        );\n    }\n\n    // Pre-allocate per-thread buffer pools to avoid per-AIR mutex contention.\n    let thread_buffers: Vec<GkrThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n        .map(|_| GkrThreadBuffers {\n            intermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_intermediates_len),\n            public_values: if max_public_values_len > 0 {\n                DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_public_values_len)\n            } else {\n                DeviceBuffer::new()\n            },\n            partition_ptrs: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_partition_ptrs_len),\n            tmp: if max_tmp_len > 0 {\n                DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_tmp_len)\n            } else {\n                DeviceBuffer::new()\n            },\n        })\n        .collect();\n\n    if num_threads <= 1 {\n        let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n        for w in &work_items {\n            process_gkr_input_air(w, &mut bufs)?;\n        }\n    } else {\n        let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n        std::thread::scope(|s| {\n            let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n                .into_iter()\n                .zip(work_items.chunks(chunk_size))\n                .map(|(mut bufs, chunk)| {\n                    s.spawn(move || -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n                        for w in chunk {\n                            process_gkr_input_air(w, &mut bufs)?;\n                        }\n                        current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n                        Ok(())\n                    })\n                })\n                .collect();\n            for handle in handles {\n                handle.join().unwrap()?;\n            }\n            Ok::<_, InteractionGpuError>(())\n        })?;\n    }\n\n    // NOTE: alpha is NO LONGER applied here - it will be fused into the first tree layer\n    // in fractional_sumcheck_gpu for better performance (eliminates one memory pass)\n    Ok((leaves, alpha_logup))\n}","numLines":140,"startLine":215,"totalLines":355}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MEnSeWMQ6GWhCTYE1B4Zxq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of the GKR pre-alloc pattern. Let me create the plan now.\n\nThe GKR pre-alloc pattern:\n1. Pre-compute max buffer sizes across all work items\n2. Memory budget check (reduce threads if needed)\n3. Pre-allocate per-thread buffer pools\n4. Pass buffer references to per-AIR processing function\n\nFor Round 0, I need to apply the same pattern, but with an adaptive threshold:\n1. Pre-compute per-AIR buffer sizes\n2. Determine a threshold (e.g., 95th percentile or budget-based)\n\n\n3. Pre-allocate per-thread buffers sized for the threshold\n4. AIRs that fit use the pre-allocated buffers without mutex contention, while those exceeding the threshold fall back to dynamic allocation\n\nThe key buffers I need to manage in Round 0's per-AIR processing are the intermediates buffer for zerocheck and the temp sums buffer, both sized based on their respective computation functions.\n\nFor the logup phase, I'm tracking the spectral evaluations buffer which persists across computations, along with intermediates and temp sums buffers specific to logup's fractional element type, plus the encoded rules and weight buffers that get transferred to device memory per AIR.\n\nLooking at the actual execution flow, I see that `process_air_round0` allocates `d_main_parts` first, then calls the GPU constraint evaluation which internally manages its own intermediates and temp buffers, followed by a device-to-host copy for zerocheck processing, and finally the interaction evaluation which allocates its own set of intermediates and spectral evaluation buffers. The key insight is that the intermediates and temp sums are the most memory-intensive and would benefit most from pre-allocation, while the result buffers need to persist beyond the function scope so they can't be easily recycled. The intermediates and temp buffers are truly temporary—they're dropped right after the kernel finishes, so they can be pre-allocated and reused across different AIRs. The result buffers (sp_evals and s_evals) need to stay valid through the D2H copy, but since the copy happens immediately on the same stream and completes before the next AIR starts, we can reuse those buffers too as long as we've copied the data out first. Let me trace through the actual code to confirm this works. I'm realizing that all the buffers used in `process_air_round0` can be pre-allocated and reused across AIR iterations since the GPU data gets copied to the host before each new AIR starts. The main challenge now is figuring out how `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` fits into this allocation strategy.\n\nI'll follow the same pattern that worked for GKR: modify the Round 0 functions to accept a pre-allocated buffer struct instead of allocating internally. This means defining a `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct that holds all the GPU buffers needed for the zerocheck and logup operations, then passing it mutably to the evaluation functions.\n\nDefining the buffer struct... I'm realizing the key constraint is that buffer sizes depend on runtime parameters and vary per AIR, so I need to compute them dynamically. The strategy is to set a reasonable threshold like 128MB per thread for intermediates, pre-allocate up to that limit, and fall back to dynamic allocation when an AIR exceeds it. I'm weighing two approaches: a threshold-based strategy that computes per-AIR buffer sizes and adapts allocation, versus a simpler fixed budget approach where I set a 128MB per-thread limit and let the kernel handle overflow with dynamic allocation. The simpler approach is more practical since the `max_temp_bytes` parameter already controls how many cosets fit in a single pass, trading off batch size for iteration count.\n\nThe key insight is that I can pre-allocate a moderate buffer per thread and pass it to all AIRs—the kernel automatically adapts by processing fewer cosets at a time if needed, so there's no need for a fallback path. The tradeoff is that smaller buffers mean more passes and potentially slower performance for large AIRs, but it keeps the implementation straightforward. I'm now looking at how the current code divides the memory limit across threads to determine what that per-thread budget should be.\n\nFor the largest AIRs, a small pre-allocated buffer like 128MB could force the kernel to do 8x more passes than necessary, which could be a significant performance regression. So I do need a threshold-based approach with a fallback after all. Let me plan this out: during work item preparation, I'll pre-compute the required buffer sizes for each AIR's operations like zerocheck, then use those to decide whether to use the pre-allocated buffer or fall back to dynamic allocation. I'm realizing the cleanest approach is to add optional buffer parameters to the evaluation functions, so `process_air_round0` can pass pre-allocated buffers when available and fall back to dynamic allocation otherwise. I could follow the same pattern from the GKR approach—modify the Round 0 evaluation functions to accept pre-allocated buffers as parameters instead of allocating internally. I'm considering either adding overloaded versions of these functions or using an optional buffer struct to keep the changes minimal. I'm setting up the buffer structure to hold intermediate computations and evaluation results, then passing it mutably to the round processing function to follow the same pre-allocation pattern used in GKR.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2266,"cache_read_input_tokens":157824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2266},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id