{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016KL2EMn5jdcnhX5Uyp51sG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Round 0 orchestration\n10\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n11\t\n12\t`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n13\t\n14\tEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n15\t\n16\t### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n17\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n18\t\n19\tAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions):\n20\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n21\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n22\t3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n23\t\n24\tAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n25\t\n26\t### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n27\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n28\t\n29\tAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions):\n30\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n31\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n32\t3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n33\t4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n34\t5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n35\t6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n36\t\n37\tItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (cannot be pre-allocated). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n38\t\n39\t### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n40\t- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n41\t\n42\t### Total allocation overhead\n43\tPer AIR: ~9 mutex acquisitions (3 + 6) for items 1-3 of each function, plus ~4 more for items 4-6 and d_main_parts. Total: **~13 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n44\t\n45\tWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~16,200 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads. Each acquisition includes mutex wait + cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync + HashMap bookkeeping.\n46\t\n47\t### Why this is slow\n48\tThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~13 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n49\t\n50\t### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\n51\tThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n52\t\n53\t## Changes\n54\t\n55\t### Step 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n56\t\n57\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n58\t\n59\tAdd a struct to hold pre-allocated per-thread buffers:\n60\t\n61\t```rust\n62\tpub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n63\t    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n64\t    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n65\t    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n66\t    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n67\t    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n68\t    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n69\t    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n70\t    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n71\t    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n72\t    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n73\t    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n74\t    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n75\t    /// Capacity thresholds (to detect when fallback is needed)\n76\t    pub zc_intermediates_cap: usize,\n77\t    pub zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n78\t    pub zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n79\t    pub logup_intermediates_cap: usize,\n80\t    pub logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n81\t    pub logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n82\t}\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\t### Step 2: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n86\t\n87\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n88\t\n89\tAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct so the thread can check whether pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n90\t\n91\t```rust\n92\tstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n93\t    // ... existing fields ...\n94\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n95\t    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n96\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n97\t    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n98\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck result capacity (num_cosets_zc * skip_domain)\n99\t    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n100\t    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed\n101\t    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n102\t    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n103\t    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n104\t    /// Pre-computed logup result capacity (num_cosets_logup * skip_domain)\n105\t    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n106\t}\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\tCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926) using the same `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` / `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` FFI calls that the evaluation functions use. This requires computing `num_cosets`, `num_x`, `buffer_size` for each AIR during preparation — extract these from `single_pk.vk` which is already available.\n110\t\n111\t### Step 3: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n112\t\n113\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n114\t\n115\tAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n116\t\n117\t1. Find the per-field maximum across work items for each of the 6 buffers, but **cap** each at a per-thread budget.\n118\t2. Budget computation:\n119\t   ```\n120\t   per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)  // 256MB cap per thread\n121\t   ```\n122\t3. For each buffer, compute `prealloc_size = min(max_across_items, budget_share)`:\n123\t   - `prealloc_zc_intermed = percentile_95(zc_intermed_cap across items)`\n124\t   - Similarly for the other 5 buffers\n125\t   - Total per-thread bytes = sum of all 6 buffer sizes\n126\t   - If total exceeds per_thread_budget: scale down proportionally\n127\t4. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of buffers:\n128\t   ```rust\n129\t   let thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n130\t       .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n131\t           zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(prealloc_zc_intermed),\n132\t           // ... etc\n133\t       })\n134\t       .collect();\n135\t   ```\n136\t5. Memory budget guard: if `num_threads * total_per_thread_bytes > 2GB`, reduce `num_threads` (same pattern as GKR).\n137\t\n138\t### Step 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept optional pre-allocated buffers\n139\t\n140\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n141\t\n142\tAdd a new parameter `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals).\n143\t\n144\tWhen `prealloc` is `Some` and the pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n145\t- Use the provided buffers directly (no allocation, no mutex)\n146\t- After the kernel writes to `sp_evals`, the caller copies data to host and the buffer is ready for reuse\n147\t\n148\tWhen `prealloc` is `None` or buffers are too small:\n149\t- Fall back to the current dynamic allocation path (unchanged behavior)\n150\t\n151\tThe change is localized: replace lines 63-68 (intermediates), line 80 (temp_sums), and line 96 (sp_evals) with conditional logic that checks `prealloc`.\n152\t\n153\t### Step 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` similarly\n154\t\n155\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n156\t\n157\tAdd `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n158\t\n159\tSame pattern as Step 4: use pre-allocated buffers when available and large enough, fall back to dynamic allocation otherwise.\n160\t\n161\tNote: `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` remain dynamically allocated per AIR since they contain AIR-specific data. These 3 allocations per AIR (out of the original 6) still acquire the mutex, but this reduces contention from ~6 to ~3 per logup call.\n162\t\n163\t### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n164\t\n165\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n166\t\n167\tChange signature to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n168\t```rust\n169\tfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n170\t    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n171\t    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n172\t) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n173\t```\n174\t\n175\tInside the function:\n176\t1. Check if each required buffer size ≤ pre-allocated capacity\n177\t2. If ALL zerocheck buffers fit: pass `Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n178\t3. If ANY doesn't fit: pass `None` (dynamic fallback)\n179\t4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()` for zerocheck, the `zc_sp_evals` buffer is safe to reuse (data is on host)\n180\t5. Same pattern for logup buffers\n181\t\n182\t### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n183\t\n184\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n185\t\n186\tPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n187\t```rust\n188\tlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n189\t    .into_iter()\n190\t    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n191\t    .enumerate()\n192\t    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n193\t        let items = &work_items;\n194\t        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n195\t            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n196\t            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n197\t                .iter()\n198\t                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n199\t                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n200\t            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n201\t            Ok(results)\n202\t        })\n203\t    })\n204\t    .collect();\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\tFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n208\t\n209\t## Invariants\n210\t\n211\t1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity for the current AIR. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n212\t2. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function synchronizes the stream, ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete.\n213\t3. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively. No synchronization needed for buffer access within a thread.\n214\t4. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. The 24GB GPU has ample headroom.\n215\t5. **APC 0 behavior unchanged**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`, and pre-allocation covers the single large AIR (or falls back gracefully). No regression path.\n216\t6. **Buffer capacity vs logical length**: Pre-allocated buffers have fixed capacity. The CUDA kernel writes up to `intermed_capacity` elements but the buffer has `prealloc_capacity >= intermed_capacity` elements. The kernel uses `intermed_capacity` (not buffer capacity) for indexing, so extra capacity is harmless.\n217\t\n218\t## Measurement Plan\n219\t\n220\t### Commands\n221\t```bash\n222\t# In powdr repo:\n223\tcd results/pairing\n224\tPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n225\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n226\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc100.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc100/metrics.json --recursion\n227\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n228\tpython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n229\t```\n230\t\n231\t### Expected results\n232\t- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-230ms (17-28% improvement)\n233\t- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1375ms (3-5% improvement)\n234\t- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs, most exceed threshold or are large enough to saturate GPU regardless)\n235\t- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise of current values\n236\t\n237\t### Stability verification\n238\tRun APC 300 3 times to confirm improvement is consistent and above noise (~20ms variance).\n239\t\n240\t### Nsight validation\n241\tRun nsight on APC 300 and check:\n242\t- CUDA API call count reduction (fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync)\n243\t- Reduced mutex contention visible as reduced CPU idle time between kernel launches\n244\t\n245\t## Rollback Criteria\n246\t\n247\t1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs vs median of 3 before-runs). This is below the noise floor and indicates the optimization doesn't work.\n248\t2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms** compared to before. Any regression in other phases (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) must not exceed 30ms.\n249\t3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. The fallback path must not add meaningful overhead.\n250\t4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n251\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01X13kWbrMMUqwM2c26drgZN","session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"f85fa5d7-7703-4059-99b5-ffd3ce35e5b8","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:15:28.892Z"}
