{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sqw5C644WH4ZYemLjWi6EE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Round 0 orchestration\n10\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n11\t\n12\t`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n13\t\n14\tEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n15\t\n16\t### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n17\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n18\t\n19\tAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions):\n20\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n21\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n22\t3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n23\t\n24\tAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n25\t\n26\t### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n27\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n28\t\n29\tAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions):\n30\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n31\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n32\t3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n33\t4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n34\t5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n35\t6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n36\t\n37\tItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (cannot be pre-allocated). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n38\t\n39\t### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n40\t- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n41\t\n42\t### Total allocation overhead\n43\tPer AIR: ~9 mutex acquisitions (3 + 6) for items 1-3 of each function, plus ~4 more for items 4-6 and d_main_parts. Total: **~13 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n44\t\n45\tWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~16,200 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads. Each acquisition includes mutex wait + cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync + HashMap bookkeeping.\n46\t\n47\t### Why this is slow\n48\tThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~13 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n49\t\n50\t### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\n51\tThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n52\t\n53\t## Changes\n54\t\n55\t### Step 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n56\t\n57\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n58\t\n59\tAdd a struct to hold pre-allocated per-thread buffers:\n60\t\n61\t```rust\n62\tpub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n63\t    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n64\t    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n65\t    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n66\t    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n67\t    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n68\t    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n69\t    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n70\t    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n71\t    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n72\t    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n73\t    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n74\t    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n75\t    /// Capacity thresholds (to detect when fallback is needed)\n76\t    pub zc_intermediates_cap: usize,\n77\t    pub zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n78\t    pub zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n79\t    pub logup_intermediates_cap: usize,\n80\t    pub logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n81\t    pub logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n82\t}\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\t### Step 2: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n86\t\n87\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n88\t\n89\tAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct so the thread can check whether pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n90\t\n91\t```rust\n92\tstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n93\t    // ... existing fields ...\n94\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n95\t    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n96\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n97\t    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n98\t    /// Pre-computed zerocheck result capacity (num_cosets_zc * skip_domain)\n99\t    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n100\t    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed\n101\t    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n102\t    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n103\t    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n104\t    /// Pre-computed logup result capacity (num_cosets_logup * skip_domain)\n105\t    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n106\t}\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\tCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926) using the same `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` / `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` FFI calls that the evaluation functions use. This requires computing `num_cosets`, `num_x`, `buffer_size` for each AIR during preparation — extract these from `single_pk.vk` which is already available.\n110\t\n111\t### Step 3: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n112\t\n113\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n114\t\n115\tAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n116\t\n117\t1. Find the per-field maximum across work items for each of the 6 buffers, but **cap** each at a per-thread budget.\n118\t2. Budget computation:\n119\t   ```\n120\t   per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)  // 256MB cap per thread\n121\t   ```\n122\t3. For each buffer, compute `prealloc_size = min(max_across_items, budget_share)`:\n123\t   - `prealloc_zc_intermed = percentile_95(zc_intermed_cap across items)`\n124\t   - Similarly for the other 5 buffers\n125\t   - Total per-thread bytes = sum of all 6 buffer sizes\n126\t   - If total exceeds per_thread_budget: scale down proportionally\n127\t4. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of buffers:\n128\t   ```rust\n129\t   let thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n130\t       .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n131\t           zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(prealloc_zc_intermed),\n132\t           // ... etc\n133\t       })\n134\t       .collect();\n135\t   ```\n136\t5. Memory budget guard: if `num_threads * total_per_thread_bytes > 2GB`, reduce `num_threads` (same pattern as GKR).\n137\t\n138\t### Step 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept optional pre-allocated buffers\n139\t\n140\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n141\t\n142\tAdd a new parameter `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals).\n143\t\n144\tWhen `prealloc` is `Some` and the pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n145\t- Use the provided buffers directly (no allocation, no mutex)\n146\t- After the kernel writes to `sp_evals`, the caller copies data to host and the buffer is ready for reuse\n147\t\n148\tWhen `prealloc` is `None` or buffers are too small:\n149\t- Fall back to the current dynamic allocation path (unchanged behavior)\n150\t\n151\tThe change is localized: replace lines 63-68 (intermediates), line 80 (temp_sums), and line 96 (sp_evals) with conditional logic that checks `prealloc`.\n152\t\n153\t### Step 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` similarly\n154\t\n155\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n156\t\n157\tAdd `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n158\t\n159\tSame pattern as Step 4: use pre-allocated buffers when available and large enough, fall back to dynamic allocation otherwise.\n160\t\n161\tNote: `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` remain dynamically allocated per AIR since they contain AIR-specific data. These 3 allocations per AIR (out of the original 6) still acquire the mutex, but this reduces contention from ~6 to ~3 per logup call.\n162\t\n163\t### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n164\t\n165\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n166\t\n167\tChange signature to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n168\t```rust\n169\tfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n170\t    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n171\t    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n172\t) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n173\t```\n174\t\n175\tInside the function:\n176\t1. Check if each required buffer size ≤ pre-allocated capacity\n177\t2. If ALL zerocheck buffers fit: pass `Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n178\t3. If ANY doesn't fit: pass `None` (dynamic fallback)\n179\t4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()` for zerocheck, the `zc_sp_evals` buffer is safe to reuse (data is on host)\n180\t5. Same pattern for logup buffers\n181\t\n182\t### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n183\t\n184\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n185\t\n186\tPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n187\t```rust\n188\tlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n189\t    .into_iter()\n190\t    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n191\t    .enumerate()\n192\t    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n193\t        let items = &work_items;\n194\t        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n195\t            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n196\t            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n197\t                .iter()\n198\t                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n199\t                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n200\t            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n201\t            Ok(results)\n202\t        })\n203\t    })\n204\t    .collect();\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\tFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n208\t\n209\t## Invariants\n210\t\n211\t1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity for the current AIR. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n212\t2. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function synchronizes the stream, ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete.\n213\t3. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively. No synchronization needed for buffer access within a thread.\n214\t4. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. The 24GB GPU has ample headroom.\n215\t5. **APC 0 behavior unchanged**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`, and pre-allocation covers the single large AIR (or falls back gracefully). No regression path.\n216\t6. **Buffer capacity vs logical length**: Pre-allocated buffers have fixed capacity. The CUDA kernel writes up to `intermed_capacity` elements but the buffer has `prealloc_capacity >= intermed_capacity` elements. The kernel uses `intermed_capacity` (not buffer capacity) for indexing, so extra capacity is harmless.\n217\t\n218\t## Measurement Plan\n219\t\n220\t### Commands\n221\t```bash\n222\t# In powdr repo:\n223\tcd results/pairing\n224\tPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n225\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n226\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc100.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc100/metrics.json --recursion\n227\t$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n228\tpython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n229\t```\n230\t\n231\t### Expected results\n232\t- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-230ms (17-28% improvement)\n233\t- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1375ms (3-5% improvement)\n234\t- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs, most exceed threshold or are large enough to saturate GPU regardless)\n235\t- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise of current values\n236\t\n237\t### Stability verification\n238\tRun APC 300 3 times to confirm improvement is consistent and above noise (~20ms variance).\n239\t\n240\t### Nsight validation\n241\tRun nsight on APC 300 and check:\n242\t- CUDA API call count reduction (fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync)\n243\t- Reduced mutex contention visible as reduced CPU idle time between kernel launches\n244\t\n245\t## Rollback Criteria\n246\t\n247\t1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs vs median of 3 before-runs). This is below the noise floor and indicates the optimization doesn't work.\n248\t2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms** compared to before. Any regression in other phases (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) must not exceed 30ms.\n249\t3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. The fallback path must not add meaningful overhead.\n250\t4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n251\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"0a72712f-da94-49d9-9998-d75d900a7805","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:18:29.331Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Round 0 orchestration\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n\n`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n\nEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n\nAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n\nAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n\nAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n\nItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (cannot be pre-allocated). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n\n### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n\n### Total allocation overhead\nPer AIR: ~9 mutex acquisitions (3 + 6) for items 1-3 of each function, plus ~4 more for items 4-6 and d_main_parts. Total: **~13 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n\nWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~16,200 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads. Each acquisition includes mutex wait + cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync + HashMap bookkeeping.\n\n### Why this is slow\nThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~13 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n\n### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\nThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd a struct to hold pre-allocated per-thread buffers:\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    /// Capacity thresholds (to detect when fallback is needed)\n    pub zc_intermediates_cap: usize,\n    pub zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    pub zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n    pub logup_intermediates_cap: usize,\n    pub logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    pub logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n}\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct so the thread can check whether pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    // ... existing fields ...\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck result capacity (num_cosets_zc * skip_domain)\n    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed\n    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup result capacity (num_cosets_logup * skip_domain)\n    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n}\n```\n\nCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926) using the same `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` / `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` FFI calls that the evaluation functions use. This requires computing `num_cosets`, `num_x`, `buffer_size` for each AIR during preparation — extract these from `single_pk.vk` which is already available.\n\n### Step 3: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n\nAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n\n1. Find the per-field maximum across work items for each of the 6 buffers, but **cap** each at a per-thread budget.\n2. Budget computation:\n   ```\n   per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)  // 256MB cap per thread\n   ```\n3. For each buffer, compute `prealloc_size = min(max_across_items, budget_share)`:\n   - `prealloc_zc_intermed = percentile_95(zc_intermed_cap across items)`\n   - Similarly for the other 5 buffers\n   - Total per-thread bytes = sum of all 6 buffer sizes\n   - If total exceeds per_thread_budget: scale down proportionally\n4. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of buffers:\n   ```rust\n   let thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n       .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n           zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(prealloc_zc_intermed),\n           // ... etc\n       })\n       .collect();\n   ```\n5. Memory budget guard: if `num_threads * total_per_thread_bytes > 2GB`, reduce `num_threads` (same pattern as GKR).\n\n### Step 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept optional pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd a new parameter `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals).\n\nWhen `prealloc` is `Some` and the pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n- Use the provided buffers directly (no allocation, no mutex)\n- After the kernel writes to `sp_evals`, the caller copies data to host and the buffer is ready for reuse\n\nWhen `prealloc` is `None` or buffers are too small:\n- Fall back to the current dynamic allocation path (unchanged behavior)\n\nThe change is localized: replace lines 63-68 (intermediates), line 80 (temp_sums), and line 96 (sp_evals) with conditional logic that checks `prealloc`.\n\n### Step 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` similarly\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n\nSame pattern as Step 4: use pre-allocated buffers when available and large enough, fall back to dynamic allocation otherwise.\n\nNote: `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` remain dynamically allocated per AIR since they contain AIR-specific data. These 3 allocations per AIR (out of the original 6) still acquire the mutex, but this reduces contention from ~6 to ~3 per logup call.\n\n### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nChange signature to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n```rust\nfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n```\n\nInside the function:\n1. Check if each required buffer size ≤ pre-allocated capacity\n2. If ALL zerocheck buffers fit: pass `Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n3. If ANY doesn't fit: pass `None` (dynamic fallback)\n4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()` for zerocheck, the `zc_sp_evals` buffer is safe to reuse (data is on host)\n5. Same pattern for logup buffers\n\n### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n\nPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n```rust\nlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n    .into_iter()\n    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n    .enumerate()\n    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n        let items = &work_items;\n        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n                .iter()\n                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n            Ok(results)\n        })\n    })\n    .collect();\n```\n\nFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity for the current AIR. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n2. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function synchronizes the stream, ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete.\n3. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively. No synchronization needed for buffer access within a thread.\n4. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. The 24GB GPU has ample headroom.\n5. **APC 0 behavior unchanged**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`, and pre-allocation covers the single large AIR (or falls back gracefully). No regression path.\n6. **Buffer capacity vs logical length**: Pre-allocated buffers have fixed capacity. The CUDA kernel writes up to `intermed_capacity` elements but the buffer has `prealloc_capacity >= intermed_capacity` elements. The kernel uses `intermed_capacity` (not buffer capacity) for indexing, so extra capacity is harmless.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Commands\n```bash\n# In powdr repo:\ncd results/pairing\nPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc100.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc100/metrics.json --recursion\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\npython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n```\n\n### Expected results\n- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-230ms (17-28% improvement)\n- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1375ms (3-5% improvement)\n- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs, most exceed threshold or are large enough to saturate GPU regardless)\n- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise of current values\n\n### Stability verification\nRun APC 300 3 times to confirm improvement is consistent and above noise (~20ms variance).\n\n### Nsight validation\nRun nsight on APC 300 and check:\n- CUDA API call count reduction (fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync)\n- Reduced mutex contention visible as reduced CPU idle time between kernel launches\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs vs median of 3 before-runs). This is below the noise floor and indicates the optimization doesn't work.\n2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms** compared to before. Any regression in other phases (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) must not exceed 30ms.\n3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. The fallback path must not add meaningful overhead.\n4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n","numLines":251,"startLine":1,"totalLines":251}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TDr42rGoUnNbCZYEzB8o8e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Z6gVToKnWXT96WWoQcCm8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Round 0 orchestration\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n\n`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n\nEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n\nAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions + 3 frees = 6 total):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n\nAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n\nThe zerocheck `buffer_size` comes from `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size` (round0.rs:51-53), which is pre-computed in the proving key and available during Phase 1 work item preparation.\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n\nAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions + 6 frees = 12 total):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n\nItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (weights depend on runtime `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows`; rules depend on a DAG built per-AIR). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n\n**Critical note:** The logup `buffer_size` (round0.rs:212) is **not** available from `pk.other_data` — it comes from a `SymbolicRulesGpu` constructed dynamically inside the function (round0.rs:161-206) via `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`. This DAG is deterministic per AIR but is NOT pre-computed in `AirDataGpu`. This must be addressed (see Step 1).\n\n### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n\n### Total allocation overhead\nPer AIR: ~6 mutex acquisitions for the 3 pre-allocatable buffers in each of the 2 functions (intermediates + temp_sums + result = 3 alloc+free pairs × 2 functions = 12 mutex acquisitions). Plus ~8 more for items 4-6, d_main_parts, and their frees. Total: **~20 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n\nWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~24,920 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads.\n\n### Why this is slow\nThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~20 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n\n### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\nThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Add `logup_round0_buffer_size` to `AirDataGpu`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\nAdd a new field to `AirDataGpu` (line 24-32):\n```rust\npub struct AirDataGpu {\n    pub interaction_rules: InteractionEvalRules,\n    pub zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>,\n    pub zerocheck_mle: ConstraintOnlyRules<false>,\n    pub zerocheck_monomials: Option<ZerocheckMonomials>,\n    pub interaction_monomials: Option<InteractionMonomials>,\n    /// Buffer size for the logup round0 interaction evaluation DAG.\n    /// Computed at keygen time to allow pre-computation of buffer sizes\n    /// during Round 0 work item preparation.\n    pub logup_round0_buffer_size: u32,\n}\n```\n\nIn `AirDataGpu::new` (pkey.rs:86-114), compute this using the same logic currently in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (round0.rs:161-211):\n1. Create `SymbolicDagBuilder`, add interaction count/message expressions\n2. Sort+dedup constraint indices\n3. Build `SymbolicExpressionDag`, then `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`\n4. Store `rules.buffer_size` as `logup_round0_buffer_size`\n\nThis makes the logup `buffer_size` available from `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` during Phase 1.\n\n### Step 2: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n}\n```\n\nNo separate capacity tracking fields — the pre-allocated `DeviceBuffer.len()` IS the capacity. The caller compares the AIR's required size against `buf.len()` to decide whether to use the pre-allocated buffer.\n\n### Step 3: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct:\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    // ... existing fields ...\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// num_cosets_zc * skip_domain (zerocheck result size)\n    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed (uses logup_round0_buffer_size from Step 1)\n    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// num_cosets_logup * skip_domain (logup result size)\n    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n}\n```\n\nCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926):\n- `local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree`\n- `skip_domain = 1 << l_skip`\n- `num_x = 1 << n_lift` where `n_lift = n.max(0) as usize`\n- `num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1)` (mod.rs:166)\n- `num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg` (mod.rs:213)\n- Zerocheck `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size`\n- Logup `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (from Step 1)\n- Call `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc, max_temp_bytes)` and the other 5 FFI size functions to get actual sizes.\n\n### Step 4: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n\nAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n\n1. For each of the 6 buffer types, find the maximum across ALL work items.\n2. If the maximum for any buffer type is 0 (e.g., all AIRs have no zerocheck constraints), use capacity 1 as a sentinel (DeviceBuffer panics on size 0). Track this so the fallback path is used for those buffers.\n3. Compute total per-thread bytes from the 6 max values.\n4. Memory budget: `per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)`.\n5. If total per-thread bytes > per_thread_budget: reduce `num_threads` until it fits, same pattern as GKR (gkr_input.rs:296-303).\n6. If after reducing to `num_threads=1` it still exceeds 2GB: skip pre-allocation entirely and use the current dynamic path.\n7. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of `Round0ThreadBuffers`.\n\n### Step 5: Modify evaluation functions to accept pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n#### D2H copy handling (addresses review finding 1)\n\n`DeviceBuffer` does not distinguish capacity from logical length — `len()` returns the allocation size. `to_host_on_current_stream()` copies `len()` elements. When a pre-allocated buffer has capacity larger than the actual output, the D2H copy would transfer excess data.\n\n**Solution:** Create a correctly-sized `DeviceBuffer` view using `ManuallyDrop` for D2H copies:\n\n```rust\nuse std::mem::ManuallyDrop;\n\n/// Create a non-owning DeviceBuffer view with the correct logical length for D2H copies.\n/// SAFETY: `buf` must have capacity >= `len`, and the caller must ensure `buf` outlives the view.\nunsafe fn device_view<T>(buf: &DeviceBuffer<T>, len: usize) -> ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer<T>> {\n    ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(buf.as_mut_ptr(), len))\n}\n```\n\nThis creates a `DeviceBuffer` that points to the same GPU memory but has the correct `len` for D2H copies. `ManuallyDrop` prevents the Drop impl from freeing the pre-allocated memory.\n\n#### `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` changes\n\nAdd parameter:\n```rust\nprealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>,\n// (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals)\n```\n\nReplace allocation of `intermediates` (lines 63-68):\n```rust\nlet (mut intermediates, owns_intermediates) = if let Some((ref mut pre_inter, _, _)) = prealloc {\n    if intermed_capacity > 0 && pre_inter.len() >= intermed_capacity {\n        // Reuse pre-allocated buffer (no mutex, no alloc)\n        // SAFETY: pre_inter has capacity >= intermed_capacity\n        (unsafe { ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(pre_inter.as_mut_ptr(), intermed_capacity)) }, false)\n    } else {\n        (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity.max(1))), true)\n    }\n} else if intermed_capacity > 0 {\n    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)), true)\n} else {\n    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::new()), false)\n};\n```\n\nApply the same pattern for `temp_sums_buffer` and `sp_evals`.\n\nFor the D2H copy of `sp_evals` in the caller (`process_air_round0`, mod.rs:184):\n```rust\nlet actual_len = w.zc_sp_evals_cap;\nlet view = unsafe { device_view(&bufs.zc_sp_evals, actual_len) };\nlet q_evals = view.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n```\n\nAt function end: if `owns_intermediates`, explicitly drop (frees via mutex). If not, ManuallyDrop prevents freeing.\n\n#### `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` changes\n\nSame pattern. Add `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n\nItems 4-6 (`d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`) remain dynamically allocated. These 3 alloc+free pairs per logup call still go through the mutex. This is unavoidable since their data is AIR-specific and runtime-dependent.\n\n### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nChange signature:\n```rust\nfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n```\n\nInside the function:\n1. Check if zerocheck buffers fit:\n   ```rust\n   let zc_prealloc = if w.zc_intermed_cap <= bufs.zc_intermediates.len()\n       && w.zc_temp_sums_cap <= bufs.zc_temp_sums.len()\n       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap <= bufs.zc_sp_evals.len()\n       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap > 0\n   {\n       Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))\n   } else {\n       None\n   };\n   ```\n2. Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(..., zc_prealloc)`.\n3. For the D2H copy: if pre-allocated was used, create a `device_view` with the actual output length (`w.zc_sp_evals_cap`). If dynamic allocation was used, the buffer already has the correct length.\n4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()`, the host data is in a `Vec<EF>`. The pre-allocated GPU buffer is safe to reuse for the next AIR.\n5. Same pattern for logup buffers, using `bufs.logup_*`.\n\n### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n\nPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n```rust\nlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n    .into_iter()\n    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n    .enumerate()\n    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n        let items = &work_items;\n        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n                .iter()\n                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n            Ok(results)\n        })\n    })\n    .collect();\n```\n\nFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n2. **D2H copy correctness**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) use `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(ptr, actual_len)>` views for D2H copies, ensuring exactly the correct number of elements are transferred to host. No excess data is copied.\n3. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function calls `current_stream_sync()` (copy.rs:147), ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete before reuse.\n4. **ManuallyDrop safety**: Views created via `ManuallyDrop` never free GPU memory. Only the owning `Round0ThreadBuffers` (dropped after all threads complete) frees the pre-allocated memory.\n5. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively.\n6. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. If it still exceeds after `num_threads=1`, pre-allocation is skipped entirely.\n7. **APC 0 behavior**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`. If the single AIR's buffers exceed pre-allocated capacity, the fallback path is used.\n8. **Kernel buffer semantics**: Intermediates and temp_sums are scratch space — kernels write to them but the data is never read back to host. Using a pre-allocated buffer with capacity > required is harmless; the kernel indexes only up to `intermed_capacity`, not the buffer's allocated length.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Commands\n```bash\n# In powdr repo:\ncd results/pairing\nPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n\n# Build\ncargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n\n# Before measurements (3 runs for APC 300)\nfor i in 1 2 3; do\n  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n\n# After implementing the optimization, rebuild and re-measure:\nfor i in 1 2 3; do\n  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n\npython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300_1/metrics.json after_apc300\n```\n\n### Expected results\n- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-240ms (13-28% improvement)\n- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1385ms (3-5% improvement)\n- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs)\n- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise\n\n### Stability verification\nCompare medians of 3 before-runs vs 3 after-runs for APC 300 to confirm improvement exceeds noise (~20ms).\n\n### Nsight validation\nRun nsight on APC 300 and verify:\n- Fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync API calls in the Round 0 NVTX span\n- Reduced mutex contention visible in CPU thread timeline (fewer blocked intervals)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs). Below the noise floor.\n2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms**. Any single-phase regression (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) > 30ms.\n3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. Fallback path must not add overhead.\n4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5608,"cache_read_input_tokens":176643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5608},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"156402f5-23cb-423a-a16e-cf4295ca4a3e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Z6gVToKnWXT96WWoQcCm8","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers/plan.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"4316c5cb-023d-47b6-aab6-f3a9a643ddaa","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:20:05.536Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Round 0 orchestration\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n\n`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n\nEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n\nAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions + 3 frees = 6 total):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n\nAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n\nThe zerocheck `buffer_size` comes from `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size` (round0.rs:51-53), which is pre-computed in the proving key and available during Phase 1 work item preparation.\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n\nAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions + 6 frees = 12 total):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n\nItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (weights depend on runtime `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows`; rules depend on a DAG built per-AIR). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n\n**Critical note:** The logup `buffer_size` (round0.rs:212) is **not** available from `pk.other_data` — it comes from a `SymbolicRulesGpu` constructed dynamically inside the function (round0.rs:161-206) via `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`. This DAG is deterministic per AIR but is NOT pre-computed in `AirDataGpu`. This must be addressed (see Step 1).\n\n### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n\n### Total allocation overhead\nPer AIR: ~6 mutex acquisitions for the 3 pre-allocatable buffers in each of the 2 functions (intermediates + temp_sums + result = 3 alloc+free pairs × 2 functions = 12 mutex acquisitions). Plus ~8 more for items 4-6, d_main_parts, and their frees. Total: **~20 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n\nWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~24,920 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads.\n\n### Why this is slow\nThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~20 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n\n### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\nThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Add `logup_round0_buffer_size` to `AirDataGpu`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\nAdd a new field to `AirDataGpu` (line 24-32):\n```rust\npub struct AirDataGpu {\n    pub interaction_rules: InteractionEvalRules,\n    pub zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>,\n    pub zerocheck_mle: ConstraintOnlyRules<false>,\n    pub zerocheck_monomials: Option<ZerocheckMonomials>,\n    pub interaction_monomials: Option<InteractionMonomials>,\n    /// Buffer size for the logup round0 interaction evaluation DAG.\n    /// Computed at keygen time to allow pre-computation of buffer sizes\n    /// during Round 0 work item preparation.\n    pub logup_round0_buffer_size: u32,\n}\n```\n\nIn `AirDataGpu::new` (pkey.rs:86-114), compute this using the same logic currently in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (round0.rs:161-211):\n1. Create `SymbolicDagBuilder`, add interaction count/message expressions\n2. Sort+dedup constraint indices\n3. Build `SymbolicExpressionDag`, then `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`\n4. Store `rules.buffer_size` as `logup_round0_buffer_size`\n\nThis makes the logup `buffer_size` available from `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` during Phase 1.\n\n### Step 2: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n}\n```\n\nNo separate capacity tracking fields — the pre-allocated `DeviceBuffer.len()` IS the capacity. The caller compares the AIR's required size against `buf.len()` to decide whether to use the pre-allocated buffer.\n\n### Step 3: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct:\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    // ... existing fields ...\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// num_cosets_zc * skip_domain (zerocheck result size)\n    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed (uses logup_round0_buffer_size from Step 1)\n    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// num_cosets_logup * skip_domain (logup result size)\n    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n}\n```\n\nCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926):\n- `local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree`\n- `skip_domain = 1 << l_skip`\n- `num_x = 1 << n_lift` where `n_lift = n.max(0) as usize`\n- `num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1)` (mod.rs:166)\n- `num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg` (mod.rs:213)\n- Zerocheck `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size`\n- Logup `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (from Step 1)\n- Call `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc, max_temp_bytes)` and the other 5 FFI size functions to get actual sizes.\n\n### Step 4: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n\nAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n\n1. For each of the 6 buffer types, find the maximum across ALL work items.\n2. If the maximum for any buffer type is 0 (e.g., all AIRs have no zerocheck constraints), use capacity 1 as a sentinel (DeviceBuffer panics on size 0). Track this so the fallback path is used for those buffers.\n3. Compute total per-thread bytes from the 6 max values.\n4. Memory budget: `per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)`.\n5. If total per-thread bytes > per_thread_budget: reduce `num_threads` until it fits, same pattern as GKR (gkr_input.rs:296-303).\n6. If after reducing to `num_threads=1` it still exceeds 2GB: skip pre-allocation entirely and use the current dynamic path.\n7. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of `Round0ThreadBuffers`.\n\n### Step 5: Modify evaluation functions to accept pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n#### D2H copy handling (addresses review finding 1)\n\n`DeviceBuffer` does not distinguish capacity from logical length — `len()` returns the allocation size. `to_host_on_current_stream()` copies `len()` elements. When a pre-allocated buffer has capacity larger than the actual output, the D2H copy would transfer excess data.\n\n**Solution:** Create a correctly-sized `DeviceBuffer` view using `ManuallyDrop` for D2H copies:\n\n```rust\nuse std::mem::ManuallyDrop;\n\n/// Create a non-owning DeviceBuffer view with the correct logical length for D2H copies.\n/// SAFETY: `buf` must have capacity >= `len`, and the caller must ensure `buf` outlives the view.\nunsafe fn device_view<T>(buf: &DeviceBuffer<T>, len: usize) -> ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer<T>> {\n    ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(buf.as_mut_ptr(), len))\n}\n```\n\nThis creates a `DeviceBuffer` that points to the same GPU memory but has the correct `len` for D2H copies. `ManuallyDrop` prevents the Drop impl from freeing the pre-allocated memory.\n\n#### `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` changes\n\nAdd parameter:\n```rust\nprealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>,\n// (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals)\n```\n\nReplace allocation of `intermediates` (lines 63-68):\n```rust\nlet (mut intermediates, owns_intermediates) = if let Some((ref mut pre_inter, _, _)) = prealloc {\n    if intermed_capacity > 0 && pre_inter.len() >= intermed_capacity {\n        // Reuse pre-allocated buffer (no mutex, no alloc)\n        // SAFETY: pre_inter has capacity >= intermed_capacity\n        (unsafe { ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(pre_inter.as_mut_ptr(), intermed_capacity)) }, false)\n    } else {\n        (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity.max(1))), true)\n    }\n} else if intermed_capacity > 0 {\n    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)), true)\n} else {\n    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::new()), false)\n};\n```\n\nApply the same pattern for `temp_sums_buffer` and `sp_evals`.\n\nFor the D2H copy of `sp_evals` in the caller (`process_air_round0`, mod.rs:184):\n```rust\nlet actual_len = w.zc_sp_evals_cap;\nlet view = unsafe { device_view(&bufs.zc_sp_evals, actual_len) };\nlet q_evals = view.to_host_on_current_stream()?;\n```\n\nAt function end: if `owns_intermediates`, explicitly drop (frees via mutex). If not, ManuallyDrop prevents freeing.\n\n#### `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` changes\n\nSame pattern. Add `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n\nItems 4-6 (`d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`) remain dynamically allocated. These 3 alloc+free pairs per logup call still go through the mutex. This is unavoidable since their data is AIR-specific and runtime-dependent.\n\n### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nChange signature:\n```rust\nfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n```\n\nInside the function:\n1. Check if zerocheck buffers fit:\n   ```rust\n   let zc_prealloc = if w.zc_intermed_cap <= bufs.zc_intermediates.len()\n       && w.zc_temp_sums_cap <= bufs.zc_temp_sums.len()\n       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap <= bufs.zc_sp_evals.len()\n       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap > 0\n   {\n       Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))\n   } else {\n       None\n   };\n   ```\n2. Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(..., zc_prealloc)`.\n3. For the D2H copy: if pre-allocated was used, create a `device_view` with the actual output length (`w.zc_sp_evals_cap`). If dynamic allocation was used, the buffer already has the correct length.\n4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()`, the host data is in a `Vec<EF>`. The pre-allocated GPU buffer is safe to reuse for the next AIR.\n5. Same pattern for logup buffers, using `bufs.logup_*`.\n\n### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n\nPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n```rust\nlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n    .into_iter()\n    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n    .enumerate()\n    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n        let items = &work_items;\n        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n                .iter()\n                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n            Ok(results)\n        })\n    })\n    .collect();\n```\n\nFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n2. **D2H copy correctness**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) use `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(ptr, actual_len)>` views for D2H copies, ensuring exactly the correct number of elements are transferred to host. No excess data is copied.\n3. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function calls `current_stream_sync()` (copy.rs:147), ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete before reuse.\n4. **ManuallyDrop safety**: Views created via `ManuallyDrop` never free GPU memory. Only the owning `Round0ThreadBuffers` (dropped after all threads complete) frees the pre-allocated memory.\n5. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively.\n6. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. If it still exceeds after `num_threads=1`, pre-allocation is skipped entirely.\n7. **APC 0 behavior**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`. If the single AIR's buffers exceed pre-allocated capacity, the fallback path is used.\n8. **Kernel buffer semantics**: Intermediates and temp_sums are scratch space — kernels write to them but the data is never read back to host. Using a pre-allocated buffer with capacity > required is harmless; the kernel indexes only up to `intermed_capacity`, not the buffer's allocated length.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Commands\n```bash\n# In powdr repo:\ncd results/pairing\nPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n\n# Build\ncargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n\n# Before measurements (3 runs for APC 300)\nfor i in 1 2 3; do\n  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n\n# After implementing the optimization, rebuild and re-measure:\nfor i in 1 2 3; do\n  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n\npython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300_1/metrics.json after_apc300\n```\n\n### Expected results\n- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-240ms (13-28% improvement)\n- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1385ms (3-5% improvement)\n- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs)\n- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise\n\n### Stability verification\nCompare medians of 3 before-runs vs 3 after-runs for APC 300 to confirm improvement exceeds noise (~20ms).\n\n### Nsight validation\nRun nsight on APC 300 and verify:\n- Fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync API calls in the Round 0 NVTX span\n- Reduced mutex contention visible in CPU thread timeline (fewer blocked intervals)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs). Below the noise floor.\n2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms**. Any single-phase regression (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) > 30ms.\n3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. Fallback path must not add overhead.\n4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":17,"newStart":16,"newLines":19,"lines":[" ### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`"," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`"," ","-Allocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions):","+Allocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions + 3 frees = 6 total):"," 1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)"," 2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)"," 3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)"," "," All three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`)."," ","+The zerocheck `buffer_size` comes from `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size` (round0.rs:51-53), which is pre-computed in the proving key and available during Phase 1 work item preparation.","+"," ### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`"," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`"," ","-Allocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions):","+Allocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions + 6 frees = 12 total):"," 1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)"," 2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)"," 3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)"]},{"oldStart":34,"oldLines":30,"newStart":36,"newLines":57,"lines":[" 5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)"," 6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)"," ","-Items 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (cannot be pre-allocated). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.","+Items 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (weights depend on runtime `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows`; rules depend on a DAG built per-AIR). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated."," ","+**Critical note:** The logup `buffer_size` (round0.rs:212) is **not** available from `pk.other_data` — it comes from a `SymbolicRulesGpu` constructed dynamically inside the function (round0.rs:161-206) via `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`. This DAG is deterministic per AIR but is NOT pre-computed in `AirDataGpu`. This must be addressed (see Step 1).","+"," ### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`"," - `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements"," "," ### Total allocation overhead","-Per AIR: ~9 mutex acquisitions (3 + 6) for items 1-3 of each function, plus ~4 more for items 4-6 and d_main_parts. Total: **~13 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.","+Per AIR: ~6 mutex acquisitions for the 3 pre-allocatable buffers in each of the 2 functions (intermediates + temp_sums + result = 3 alloc+free pairs × 2 functions = 12 mutex acquisitions). Plus ~8 more for items 4-6, d_main_parts, and their frees. Total: **~20 mutex acquisitions per AIR**."," ","-With 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~16,200 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads. Each acquisition includes mutex wait + cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync + HashMap bookkeeping.","+With 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~24,920 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads."," "," ### Why this is slow","-The global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~13 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.","+The global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~20 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval."," "," ### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed"," The `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms)."," "," ## Changes"," ","-### Step 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct","+### Step 1: Add `logup_round0_buffer_size` to `AirDataGpu`"," ","-**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`","+**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`"," ","-Add a struct to hold pre-allocated per-thread buffers:","+Add a new field to `AirDataGpu` (line 24-32):","+```rust","+pub struct AirDataGpu {","+    pub interaction_rules: InteractionEvalRules,","+    pub zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>,","+    pub zerocheck_mle: ConstraintOnlyRules<false>,","+    pub zerocheck_monomials: Option<ZerocheckMonomials>,","+    pub interaction_monomials: Option<InteractionMonomials>,","+    /// Buffer size for the logup round0 interaction evaluation DAG.","+    /// Computed at keygen time to allow pre-computation of buffer sizes","+    /// during Round 0 work item preparation.","+    pub logup_round0_buffer_size: u32,","+}","+```"," ","+In `AirDataGpu::new` (pkey.rs:86-114), compute this using the same logic currently in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (round0.rs:161-211):","+1. Create `SymbolicDagBuilder`, add interaction count/message expressions","+2. Sort+dedup constraint indices","+3. Build `SymbolicExpressionDag`, then `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`","+4. Store `rules.buffer_size` as `logup_round0_buffer_size`","+","+This makes the logup `buffer_size` available from `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` during Phase 1.","+","+### Step 2: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct","+","+**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`","+"," ```rust"," pub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {","     /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)"]},{"oldStart":72,"oldLines":21,"newStart":101,"newLines":16,"lines":["     pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,","     /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup","     pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,","-    /// Capacity thresholds (to detect when fallback is needed)","-    pub zc_intermediates_cap: usize,","-    pub zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,","-    pub zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,","-    pub logup_intermediates_cap: usize,","-    pub logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,","-    pub logup_s_evals_cap: usize,"," }"," ```"," ","-### Step 2: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`","+No separate capacity tracking fields — the pre-allocated `DeviceBuffer.len()` IS the capacity. The caller compares the AIR's required size against `buf.len()` to decide whether to use the pre-allocated buffer."," ","+### Step 3: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`","+"," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-Add pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct so the thread can check whether pre-allocated buffers are large enough:","+Add pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct:"," "," ```rust"," struct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {"]},{"oldStart":95,"oldLines":76,"newStart":119,"newLines":110,"lines":["     zc_intermed_cap: usize,","     /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed","     zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,","-    /// Pre-computed zerocheck result capacity (num_cosets_zc * skip_domain)","+    /// num_cosets_zc * skip_domain (zerocheck result size)","     zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,","-    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed","+    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed (uses logup_round0_buffer_size from Step 1)","     logup_intermed_cap: usize,","     /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed","     logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,","-    /// Pre-computed logup result capacity (num_cosets_logup * skip_domain)","+    /// num_cosets_logup * skip_domain (logup result size)","     logup_s_evals_cap: usize,"," }"," ```"," ","-Compute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926) using the same `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` / `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` FFI calls that the evaluation functions use. This requires computing `num_cosets`, `num_x`, `buffer_size` for each AIR during preparation — extract these from `single_pk.vk` which is already available.","+Compute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926):","+- `local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree`","+- `skip_domain = 1 << l_skip`","+- `num_x = 1 << n_lift` where `n_lift = n.max(0) as usize`","+- `num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1)` (mod.rs:166)","+- `num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg` (mod.rs:213)","+- Zerocheck `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size`","+- Logup `buffer_size` from `single_pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (from Step 1)","+- Call `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc, max_temp_bytes)` and the other 5 FFI size functions to get actual sizes."," ","-### Step 3: Compute threshold and pre-allocate","+### Step 4: Compute threshold and pre-allocate"," "," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)"," "," After building work items with their buffer sizes:"," ","-1. Find the per-field maximum across work items for each of the 6 buffers, but **cap** each at a per-thread budget.","-2. Budget computation:","-   ```","-   per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)  // 256MB cap per thread","-   ```","-3. For each buffer, compute `prealloc_size = min(max_across_items, budget_share)`:","-   - `prealloc_zc_intermed = percentile_95(zc_intermed_cap across items)`","-   - Similarly for the other 5 buffers","-   - Total per-thread bytes = sum of all 6 buffer sizes","-   - If total exceeds per_thread_budget: scale down proportionally","-4. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of buffers:","-   ```rust","-   let thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)","-       .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {","-           zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(prealloc_zc_intermed),","-           // ... etc","-       })","-       .collect();","-   ```","-5. Memory budget guard: if `num_threads * total_per_thread_bytes > 2GB`, reduce `num_threads` (same pattern as GKR).","+1. For each of the 6 buffer types, find the maximum across ALL work items.","+2. If the maximum for any buffer type is 0 (e.g., all AIRs have no zerocheck constraints), use capacity 1 as a sentinel (DeviceBuffer panics on size 0). Track this so the fallback path is used for those buffers.","+3. Compute total per-thread bytes from the 6 max values.","+4. Memory budget: `per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)`.","+5. If total per-thread bytes > per_thread_budget: reduce `num_threads` until it fits, same pattern as GKR (gkr_input.rs:296-303).","+6. If after reducing to `num_threads=1` it still exceeds 2GB: skip pre-allocation entirely and use the current dynamic path.","+7. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of `Round0ThreadBuffers`."," ","-### Step 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept optional pre-allocated buffers","+### Step 5: Modify evaluation functions to accept pre-allocated buffers"," "," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`"," ","-Add a new parameter `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals).","+#### D2H copy handling (addresses review finding 1)"," ","-When `prealloc` is `Some` and the pre-allocated buffers are large enough:","-- Use the provided buffers directly (no allocation, no mutex)","-- After the kernel writes to `sp_evals`, the caller copies data to host and the buffer is ready for reuse","+`DeviceBuffer` does not distinguish capacity from logical length — `len()` returns the allocation size. `to_host_on_current_stream()` copies `len()` elements. When a pre-allocated buffer has capacity larger than the actual output, the D2H copy would transfer excess data."," ","-When `prealloc` is `None` or buffers are too small:","-- Fall back to the current dynamic allocation path (unchanged behavior)","+**Solution:** Create a correctly-sized `DeviceBuffer` view using `ManuallyDrop` for D2H copies:"," ","-The change is localized: replace lines 63-68 (intermediates), line 80 (temp_sums), and line 96 (sp_evals) with conditional logic that checks `prealloc`.","+```rust","+use std::mem::ManuallyDrop;"," ","-### Step 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` similarly","+/// Create a non-owning DeviceBuffer view with the correct logical length for D2H copies.","+/// SAFETY: `buf` must have capacity >= `len`, and the caller must ensure `buf` outlives the view.","+unsafe fn device_view<T>(buf: &DeviceBuffer<T>, len: usize) -> ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer<T>> {","+    ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(buf.as_mut_ptr(), len))","+}","+```"," ","-**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`","+This creates a `DeviceBuffer` that points to the same GPU memory but has the correct `len` for D2H copies. `ManuallyDrop` prevents the Drop impl from freeing the pre-allocated memory."," ","-Add `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).","+#### `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` changes"," ","-Same pattern as Step 4: use pre-allocated buffers when available and large enough, fall back to dynamic allocation otherwise.","+Add parameter:","+```rust","+prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>,","+// (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals)","+```"," ","-Note: `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` remain dynamically allocated per AIR since they contain AIR-specific data. These 3 allocations per AIR (out of the original 6) still acquire the mutex, but this reduces contention from ~6 to ~3 per logup call.","+Replace allocation of `intermediates` (lines 63-68):","+```rust","+let (mut intermediates, owns_intermediates) = if let Some((ref mut pre_inter, _, _)) = prealloc {","+    if intermed_capacity > 0 && pre_inter.len() >= intermed_capacity {","+        // Reuse pre-allocated buffer (no mutex, no alloc)","+        // SAFETY: pre_inter has capacity >= intermed_capacity","+        (unsafe { ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(pre_inter.as_mut_ptr(), intermed_capacity)) }, false)","+    } else {","+        (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity.max(1))), true)","+    }","+} else if intermed_capacity > 0 {","+    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)), true)","+} else {","+    (ManuallyDrop::new(DeviceBuffer::<F>::new()), false)","+};","+```"," ","+Apply the same pattern for `temp_sums_buffer` and `sp_evals`.","+","+For the D2H copy of `sp_evals` in the caller (`process_air_round0`, mod.rs:184):","+```rust","+let actual_len = w.zc_sp_evals_cap;","+let view = unsafe { device_view(&bufs.zc_sp_evals, actual_len) };","+let q_evals = view.to_host_on_current_stream()?;","+```","+","+At function end: if `owns_intermediates`, explicitly drop (frees via mutex). If not, ManuallyDrop prevents freeing.","+","+#### `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` changes","+","+Same pattern. Add `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).","+","+Items 4-6 (`d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`) remain dynamically allocated. These 3 alloc+free pairs per logup call still go through the mutex. This is unavoidable since their data is AIR-specific and runtime-dependent.","+"," ### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers"," "," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-Change signature to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:","+Change signature:"," ```rust"," fn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(","     w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,"]},{"oldStart":173,"oldLines":11,"newStart":231,"newLines":22,"lines":[" ```"," "," Inside the function:","-1. Check if each required buffer size ≤ pre-allocated capacity","-2. If ALL zerocheck buffers fit: pass `Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`","-3. If ANY doesn't fit: pass `None` (dynamic fallback)","-4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()` for zerocheck, the `zc_sp_evals` buffer is safe to reuse (data is on host)","-5. Same pattern for logup buffers","+1. Check if zerocheck buffers fit:","+   ```rust","+   let zc_prealloc = if w.zc_intermed_cap <= bufs.zc_intermediates.len()","+       && w.zc_temp_sums_cap <= bufs.zc_temp_sums.len()","+       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap <= bufs.zc_sp_evals.len()","+       && w.zc_sp_evals_cap > 0","+   {","+       Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))","+   } else {","+       None","+   };","+   ```","+2. Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(..., zc_prealloc)`.","+3. For the D2H copy: if pre-allocated was used, create a `device_view` with the actual output length (`w.zc_sp_evals_cap`). If dynamic allocation was used, the buffer already has the correct length.","+4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()`, the host data is in a `Vec<EF>`. The pre-allocated GPU buffer is safe to reuse for the next AIR.","+5. Same pattern for logup buffers, using `bufs.logup_*`."," "," ### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn"," "]},{"oldStart":208,"oldLines":12,"newStart":277,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," ## Invariants"," ","-1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity for the current AIR. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.","-2. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function synchronizes the stream, ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete.","-3. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively. No synchronization needed for buffer access within a thread.","-4. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. The 24GB GPU has ample headroom.","-5. **APC 0 behavior unchanged**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`, and pre-allocation covers the single large AIR (or falls back gracefully). No regression path.","-6. **Buffer capacity vs logical length**: Pre-allocated buffers have fixed capacity. The CUDA kernel writes up to `intermed_capacity` elements but the buffer has `prealloc_capacity >= intermed_capacity` elements. The kernel uses `intermed_capacity` (not buffer capacity) for indexing, so extra capacity is harmless.","+1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.","+2. **D2H copy correctness**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) use `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer::from_raw_parts(ptr, actual_len)>` views for D2H copies, ensuring exactly the correct number of elements are transferred to host. No excess data is copied.","+3. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function calls `current_stream_sync()` (copy.rs:147), ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete before reuse.","+4. **ManuallyDrop safety**: Views created via `ManuallyDrop` never free GPU memory. Only the owning `Round0ThreadBuffers` (dropped after all threads complete) frees the pre-allocated memory.","+5. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively.","+6. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. If it still exceeds after `num_threads=1`, pre-allocation is skipped entirely.","+7. **APC 0 behavior**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`. If the single AIR's buffers exceed pre-allocated capacity, the fallback path is used.","+8. **Kernel buffer semantics**: Intermediates and temp_sums are scratch space — kernels write to them but the data is never read back to host. Using a pre-allocated buffer with capacity > required is harmless; the kernel indexes only up to `intermed_capacity`, not the buffer's allocated length."," "," ## Measurement Plan"," "]},{"oldStart":222,"oldLines":29,"newStart":293,"newLines":42,"lines":[" # In powdr repo:"," cd results/pairing"," PROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"","-$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion","-$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc100.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc100/metrics.json --recursion","+","+# Build","+cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"","+","+# Before measurements (3 runs for APC 300)","+for i in 1 2 3; do","+  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion","+done","+$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics before_apc000/metrics.json --recursion","+","+# After implementing the optimization, rebuild and re-measure:","+for i in 1 2 3; do","+  $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300_$i/metrics.json --recursion","+done"," $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion","-python3 ~/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300","+","+python3 ~/spec.py after_apc300_1/metrics.json after_apc300"," ```"," "," ### Expected results","-- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-230ms (17-28% improvement)","-- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1375ms (3-5% improvement)","-- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs, most exceed threshold or are large enough to saturate GPU regardless)","-- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise of current values","+- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-240ms (13-28% improvement)","+- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1385ms (3-5% improvement)","+- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs)","+- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise"," "," ### Stability verification","-Run APC 300 3 times to confirm improvement is consistent and above noise (~20ms variance).","+Compare medians of 3 before-runs vs 3 after-runs for APC 300 to confirm improvement exceeds noise (~20ms)."," "," ### Nsight validation","-Run nsight on APC 300 and check:","-- CUDA API call count reduction (fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync)","-- Reduced mutex contention visible as reduced CPU idle time between kernel launches","+Run nsight on APC 300 and verify:","+- Fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync API calls in the Round 0 NVTX span","+- Reduced mutex contention visible in CPU thread timeline (fewer blocked intervals)"," "," ## Rollback Criteria"," ","-1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs vs median of 3 before-runs). This is below the noise floor and indicates the optimization doesn't work.","-2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms** compared to before. Any regression in other phases (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) must not exceed 30ms.","-3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. The fallback path must not add meaningful overhead.","+1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs). Below the noise floor.","+2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms**. Any single-phase regression (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) > 30ms.","+3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. Fallback path must not add overhead."," 4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed)."]}],"originalFile":"# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread Round 0 buffers with adaptive size threshold\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR GPU memory allocation overhead in the Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread buffer pools, following the pattern that saved 217ms in GKR input evaluation (`prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`). Use an adaptive size threshold to avoid the GPU memory pressure that caused the previous Round 0 pre-allocation attempt (`prealloc-round0-buffers`) to fail.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Round 0 orchestration\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:767-1003`\n\n`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` processes 623 AIRs (at APC 300) across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Work items are sorted by descending height and distributed round-robin.\n\nEach thread calls `process_air_round0` (mod.rs:140-272) per AIR, which calls two evaluation functions sequentially:\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n\nAllocations per call (3 mutex acquisitions):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 96)\n\nAll three are freed on function return (Drop). Each alloc/free pair acquires the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex (`crates/cuda-common/src/memory_manager/mod.rs:30`).\n\n### Per-AIR evaluation: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-274`\n\nAllocations per call (6 mutex acquisitions):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n3. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` — size = `num_cosets * skip_domain` (line 248)\n4. `d_rules` — from `encoded_rules.to_device()` (line 210)\n5. `d_numer_weights` — from `numer_weights.to_device()` (line 204)\n6. `d_denom_weights` — from `denom_weights.to_device()` (line 205)\n\nItems 4-6 are data-dependent per AIR (cannot be pre-allocated). Items 1-3 can be pre-allocated.\n\n### Additional per-AIR allocations in `process_air_round0`\n- `d_main_parts` — from `main_parts.to_device()` (mod.rs:162), ~8-16 elements\n\n### Total allocation overhead\nPer AIR: ~9 mutex acquisitions (3 + 6) for items 1-3 of each function, plus ~4 more for items 4-6 and d_main_parts. Total: **~13 mutex acquisitions per AIR**.\n\nWith 623 AIRs × 2 segments = 1246 AIR evaluations: **~16,200 mutex acquisitions** across 8 concurrent threads. Each acquisition includes mutex wait + cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync + HashMap bookkeeping.\n\n### Why this is slow\nThe global `MEMORY_MANAGER` singleton (`Mutex<MemoryManager>`, mod.rs:30 of cuda-common) serializes all allocations across all threads. With 8 concurrent threads each doing ~13 alloc/free cycles per AIR, the mutex is heavily contended. The GKR pre-alloc optimization proved this pattern: eliminating ~1,240 mutex acquisitions per segment saved 214ms for GKR input eval.\n\n### Why the previous Round 0 pre-alloc failed\nThe `prealloc-round0-buffers` attempt pre-allocated for the **maximum** AIR across all work items. The max intermediates buffer was ~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB, which caused systemic GPU memory pressure (only 24GB total) that degraded all phases including GKR (+188ms) and Leaf Recursion (+100ms).\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd a struct to hold pre-allocated per-thread buffers:\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for zerocheck (reused across AIRs)\n    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for zerocheck\n    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for zerocheck (data copied to host before reuse)\n    pub zc_sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated intermediates buffer for logup\n    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated temp sums buffer for logup\n    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    /// Pre-allocated result buffer for logup\n    pub logup_s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    /// Capacity thresholds (to detect when fallback is needed)\n    pub zc_intermediates_cap: usize,\n    pub zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    pub zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n    pub logup_intermediates_cap: usize,\n    pub logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    pub logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n}\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add buffer size fields to `Round0AirWorkItem`\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd pre-computed buffer sizes to the work item struct so the thread can check whether pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    // ... existing fields ...\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck intermediates capacity needed\n    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck temp sums capacity needed\n    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed zerocheck result capacity (num_cosets_zc * skip_domain)\n    zc_sp_evals_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup intermediates capacity needed\n    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup temp sums capacity needed\n    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    /// Pre-computed logup result capacity (num_cosets_logup * skip_domain)\n    logup_s_evals_cap: usize,\n}\n```\n\nCompute these during Phase 1 (work item preparation, mod.rs ~901-926) using the same `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` / `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` FFI calls that the evaluation functions use. This requires computing `num_cosets`, `num_x`, `buffer_size` for each AIR during preparation — extract these from `single_pk.vk` which is already available.\n\n### Step 3: Compute threshold and pre-allocate\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, between Phase 1 and Phase 2)\n\nAfter building work items with their buffer sizes:\n\n1. Find the per-field maximum across work items for each of the 6 buffers, but **cap** each at a per-thread budget.\n2. Budget computation:\n   ```\n   per_thread_budget = min(memory_limit_bytes / num_threads, 256 * 1024 * 1024)  // 256MB cap per thread\n   ```\n3. For each buffer, compute `prealloc_size = min(max_across_items, budget_share)`:\n   - `prealloc_zc_intermed = percentile_95(zc_intermed_cap across items)`\n   - Similarly for the other 5 buffers\n   - Total per-thread bytes = sum of all 6 buffer sizes\n   - If total exceeds per_thread_budget: scale down proportionally\n4. Pre-allocate `num_threads` sets of buffers:\n   ```rust\n   let thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n       .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n           zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(prealloc_zc_intermed),\n           // ... etc\n       })\n       .collect();\n   ```\n5. Memory budget guard: if `num_threads * total_per_thread_bytes > 2GB`, reduce `num_threads` (same pattern as GKR).\n\n### Step 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept optional pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd a new parameter `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals).\n\nWhen `prealloc` is `Some` and the pre-allocated buffers are large enough:\n- Use the provided buffers directly (no allocation, no mutex)\n- After the kernel writes to `sp_evals`, the caller copies data to host and the buffer is ready for reuse\n\nWhen `prealloc` is `None` or buffers are too small:\n- Fall back to the current dynamic allocation path (unchanged behavior)\n\nThe change is localized: replace lines 63-68 (intermediates), line 80 (temp_sums), and line 96 (sp_evals) with conditional logic that checks `prealloc`.\n\n### Step 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` similarly\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd `prealloc: Option<(&mut DeviceBuffer<F>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>)>` for (intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals).\n\nSame pattern as Step 4: use pre-allocated buffers when available and large enough, fall back to dynamic allocation otherwise.\n\nNote: `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` remain dynamically allocated per AIR since they contain AIR-specific data. These 3 allocations per AIR (out of the original 6) still acquire the mutex, but this reduces contention from ~6 to ~3 per logup call.\n\n### Step 6: Modify `process_air_round0` to use pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nChange signature to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n```rust\nfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n    bufs: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError>\n```\n\nInside the function:\n1. Check if each required buffer size ≤ pre-allocated capacity\n2. If ALL zerocheck buffers fit: pass `Some((&mut bufs.zc_intermediates, &mut bufs.zc_temp_sums, &mut bufs.zc_sp_evals))` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n3. If ANY doesn't fit: pass `None` (dynamic fallback)\n4. After `to_host_on_current_stream()` for zerocheck, the `zc_sp_evals` buffer is safe to reuse (data is on host)\n5. Same pattern for logup buffers\n\n### Step 7: Wire up pre-allocated buffers in the thread spawn\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (Phase 2, lines 963-985)\n\nPass one `Round0ThreadBuffers` to each spawned thread:\n```rust\nlet handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n    .into_iter()\n    .zip(thread_items.into_iter())\n    .enumerate()\n    .map(|(thread_id, (mut bufs, indices))| {\n        let items = &work_items;\n        s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n            let t0 = std::time::Instant::now();\n            let results: Vec<_> = indices\n                .iter()\n                .map(|&idx| process_air_round0(&items[idx], &mut bufs))\n                .collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n            tracing::debug!(thread_id, elapsed_ms = t0.elapsed().as_millis(), num_airs = indices.len(), \"round0 thread done\");\n            Ok(results)\n        })\n    })\n    .collect();\n```\n\nFor the single-thread path (`num_threads <= 1`), pass the single buffer set similarly.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers are only used when they meet or exceed the required capacity for the current AIR. When they don't fit, the fallback path is identical to the current code.\n2. **Buffer reuse safety**: Result buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) are only reused after `to_host_on_current_stream()` completes. This function synchronizes the stream, ensuring all GPU operations on the buffer are complete.\n3. **No cross-thread sharing**: Each thread owns its buffer set exclusively. No synchronization needed for buffer access within a thread.\n4. **Memory budget**: Total pre-allocation is bounded by `min(256MB × num_threads, 2GB)`. If this exceeds budget, `num_threads` is reduced. The 24GB GPU has ample headroom.\n5. **APC 0 behavior unchanged**: With < 100 AIRs, `num_threads = 1`, and pre-allocation covers the single large AIR (or falls back gracefully). No regression path.\n6. **Buffer capacity vs logical length**: Pre-allocated buffers have fixed capacity. The CUDA kernel writes up to `intermed_capacity` elements but the buffer has `prealloc_capacity >= intermed_capacity` elements. The kernel uses `intermed_capacity` (not buffer capacity) for indexing, so extra capacity is harmless.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Commands\n```bash\n# In powdr repo:\ncd results/pairing\nPROVE_BIN=\"$(cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps 2>/dev/null | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"target_directory\"])')/release/powdr_openvm_riscv\"\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc100.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc100/metrics.json --recursion\n$PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\npython3 ~/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n```\n\n### Expected results\n- **Round 0 at APC 300**: 276ms → 200-230ms (17-28% improvement)\n- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1421ms → 1345-1375ms (3-5% improvement)\n- **Round 0 at APC 0**: 177ms → 177ms (no change — single-threaded, few AIRs, most exceed threshold or are large enough to saturate GPU regardless)\n- **No regression in other phases**: GKR, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings should be within noise of current values\n\n### Stability verification\nRun APC 300 3 times to confirm improvement is consistent and above noise (~20ms variance).\n\n### Nsight validation\nRun nsight on APC 300 and check:\n- CUDA API call count reduction (fewer cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync)\n- Reduced mutex contention visible as reduced CPU idle time between kernel launches\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n1. **Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 20ms** (median of 3 runs vs median of 3 before-runs). This is below the noise floor and indicates the optimization doesn't work.\n2. **STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms** compared to before. Any regression in other phases (GKR, Trace Commit, Openings) must not exceed 30ms.\n3. **APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 30ms**. The fallback path must not add meaningful overhead.\n4. **Any correctness failure** at any APC configuration (prove + verify must succeed).\n"}}
