{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXy8VNDxGfsQobBQZXT9Xu","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers\n\nPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation using an adaptive size threshold, rather than pre-allocating for the maximum AIR size. The previous pre-allocation attempt (prealloc-round0-buffers) failed because it pre-allocated for the largest AIR's intermediates (~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB), causing systemic GPU memory pressure that degraded all phases. The adaptive approach pre-allocates buffers sized for the Nth-percentile AIR (e.g., 95th percentile), covering 95%+ of AIRs while keeping total allocation manageable. Small/medium AIRs (the vast majority at APC 300) skip the global MEMORY_MANAGER mutex entirely, while the few large AIRs fall back to dynamic allocation. This addresses the same root cause as the successful GKR pre-alloc optimization (which saved 217ms): eliminating per-AIR mutex contention and cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync serialization across 8 concurrent worker threads.\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 17904 Apr 13 22:20 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current measurements ===\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc000/metrics.json\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc100/metrics.json\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc300/metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc300/nsys_report.nsys-rep","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a79019c-b2e6-4f68-9275-45a371b42d97","uuid":"0cbe1041-44a3-4dab-abc3-8f9e5bb21075","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:23:03.842Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers\n\nPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation using an adaptive size threshold, rather than pre-allocating for the maximum AIR size. The previous pre-allocation attempt (prealloc-round0-buffers) failed because it pre-allocated for the largest AIR's intermediates (~1GB per thread × 8 threads = 8GB), causing systemic GPU memory pressure that degraded all phases. The adaptive approach pre-allocates buffers sized for the Nth-percentile AIR (e.g., 95th percentile), covering 95%+ of AIRs while keeping total allocation manageable. Small/medium AIRs (the vast majority at APC 300) skip the global MEMORY_MANAGER mutex entirely, while the few large AIRs fall back to dynamic allocation. This addresses the same root cause as the successful GKR pre-alloc optimization (which saved 217ms): eliminating per-AIR mutex contention and cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync serialization across 8 concurrent worker threads.\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 17904 Apr 13 22:20 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2200-prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current measurements ===\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc000/metrics.json\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc100/metrics.json\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc300/metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/powdr/results/pairing/current_apc300/nsys_report.nsys-rep","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
